  if (slug === 'jaipur-same-day-sightseeing-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What exactly is included in the price of this tour?", answer: "Your **399 USD** covers a private air-conditioned car with an experienced driver for the full **10 hours**, a professional Govt.-approved tour guide, **entry fees to all the monuments** on the itinerary, **lunch**, and bottled water throughout the day. There are no hidden extras for the sightseeing itself, so the only things you'd pay out of pocket are personal shopping, tips, and any snacks or drinks beyond what's provided." },
      { question: "Which Jaipur landmarks does this tour actually cover?", answer: "You'll visit the **Amber Fort** with its grand courtyards and mirror work, stop for photos at the **Jal Mahal** (the water palace on Man Sagar Lake), tour the **City Palace** with its museums and royal artifacts, and admire the honeycomb façade of the **Hawa Mahal**. There's also time to stroll Jaipur's colourful bazaars for handicrafts, textiles, and jewellery. If you'd like landmarks like Jantar Mantar added, our [Iconic Landmarks Tour](/india/jaipur/hawa-mahal-landmarks-guided-tour) focuses on those observatory and palace highlights." },
      { question: "Do you pick me up from my hotel?", answer: "Yes. The tour includes **private car pick-up and drop-off** from your hotel or accommodation anywhere in Jaipur. Your driver arrives directly at your door, so there's no meeting point to find. When you book, just share your hotel name and preferred start time and we'll confirm the pickup with your guide the evening before." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or will I share it with strangers?", answer: "This is a fully **private tour** — the car, driver, and guide are exclusively yours for the day. That means you set the pace, spend longer at the sites you love, and skip anything that doesn't interest you. It's ideal for couples, families, or small groups who want a flexible day rather than a fixed coach schedule." },
      { question: "How physically demanding is the day, and is there a lot of walking?", answer: "Most of the day is comfortable, but the **Amber Fort involves a steep uphill climb** to the main entrance and plenty of stairs and ramps inside. The **City Palace** and the bazaars around Hawa Mahal also mean a fair amount of walking on uneven ground. Wear supportive shoes and take your time — your guide will pace things to suit you, and the private car means you can rest between stops." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for young children and older travellers?", answer: "Absolutely. Because it's private and travels by air-conditioned car, families with kids and older travellers can go at a relaxed pace with rest stops whenever needed. The only real consideration is the **climb up to Amber Fort** — older guests can hire a jeep to the top for a small extra fee, and your guide will happily arrange it on the day." },
      { question: "When is the best time of day and year to do this tour?", answer: "An **early start (around 8–9 am)** is best so you reach Amber Fort before the midday heat and the biggest tour crowds. The most comfortable months are **October to March**, when Jaipur's days are pleasantly warm. From April to June it can climb past 40°C, so we schedule the outdoor forts first and indoor palaces and shaded bazaars for the hotter afternoon." },
      { question: "How should I dress for the Jaipur heat and the monuments?", answer: "Wear **light, breathable clothing**, comfortable walking shoes for the Amber Fort climb, and bring a hat and sunglasses. Sunscreen is essential in the Pink City sun. For the City Palace and other heritage sites, modest clothing that covers shoulders and knees is respectful and comfortable. We provide **bottled water** all day, but staying hydrated is key from April through June." },
      { question: "Are the monument entry tickets already covered, so I skip the ticket queues?", answer: "Yes — **entry fees to the monuments on the itinerary are included** in the 399 USD price, so you won't be buying tickets at each gate. Your Govt.-approved guide handles entry so you spend your time exploring rather than queuing. If you'd prefer a guide-only arrangement where you pay entries separately, our [official guide booking option](/india/jaipur/jaipur-city-tour-with-official-guide) is an alternative." },
      { question: "Can I take photos inside the palaces and forts?", answer: "Photography is wonderful here — the **Hawa Mahal** façade at morning light and the mirrored halls of **Amber Fort** are highlights. Most sites allow photos, though a few interior museum galleries at the **City Palace** restrict cameras or charge a small camera fee, which your guide will point out. Your driver knows the best angle across the lake for that classic **Jal Mahal** shot too." },
      { question: "Will there be time for shopping, and can my guide help me bargain?", answer: "Yes, the itinerary includes a stroll through Jaipur's markets for **handicrafts, textiles, and jewellery**, and your guide can help you navigate prices and avoid overpaying. If shopping is your main interest, you might prefer our dedicated [Craft & Shopping Experience with blue pottery and textile printing](/india/jaipur/jaipur-shopping-tour), which goes deeper into artisan workshops and hands-on demonstrations." },
      { question: "What's included for lunch, and can you cater to vegetarians?", answer: "**Lunch is included** and served at a good local restaurant during the tour. India, and Rajasthan especially, is very vegetarian-friendly, so pure-veg, Jain, or vegan meals are no problem — just let us know your preference when booking. If you'd love to go further into Rajasthani food, consider adding the [Same Day Jaipur Tour with a cooking class](/india/jaipur/jaipur-same-day-tour-with-cooking-class)." },
      { question: "How long is the tour, and can I customise the itinerary?", answer: "The tour runs about **10 hours**, which comfortably covers Amber Fort, Jal Mahal, City Palace, Hawa Mahal, and the markets at an unhurried pace. Because it's private, you can adjust the flow — spend longer at a favourite site or add a quick stop like Albert Hall or Nahargarh Fort. Just discuss it with your guide on the day and they'll do their best to fit it in." },
      { question: "Is this the same as a full-day sightseeing tour, and how do I choose?", answer: "This same-day tour is essentially a complete full-day experience covering Jaipur's headline monuments in one convenient package with car, guide, entries, and lunch. If you want a very similar itinerary framed differently, our [Private Full Day Sightseeing Tour by car with guide](/india/jaipur/jaipur-full-day-sightseeing-tour-by-car) is a close alternative. This tour is the best fit for travellers with a single day who want everything sorted end to end." },
      { question: "What is the cancellation policy?", answer: "You can **cancel free of charge up to 24 hours** before your scheduled start time for a full refund. Cancellations within 24 hours are non-refundable because the private car and guide are reserved exclusively for you. If your plans are uncertain, book anyway and adjust later — we'll always try to help with rescheduling where possible." },
      { question: "How do I book and confirm this tour?", answer: "Simply select the **Same Day Jaipur Sightseeing Tour** option at **399 USD** and complete your booking online. After that we confirm your **hotel pickup time and location**, note any dietary or accessibility needs, and share your guide's details before the tour. You'll receive a confirmation with everything you need, and our team is on hand for any questions right up to your travel day." },
    ];
  }

  // --- JAIPUR: hawa-mahal-full-day-tour (auto-added 2026-07-02) ---
  if (slug === 'hawa-mahal-full-day-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What exactly does this full-day tour cover in 8 hours?", answer: "This is a **full-day private tour (8 hours)** designed to see Jaipur's headline sights at a comfortable pace. Your guide covers the Amber Fort and Palace (about 2 hours), the historic **Panna Meena Ka Kund** stepwell, and the beautiful **Jal Mahal** (\"Water Palace\") floating on Man Sagar Lake, alongside the Pink City classics like Hawa Mahal, City Palace and Jantar Mantar. Everything moves in a comfortable AC car so you spend your energy sightseeing, not walking between stops." },
      { question: "Is hotel pickup and drop-off included?", answer: "Yes. **Hotel pickup and drop-off are included**, so your driver will collect you directly from your Jaipur hotel or guesthouse at your agreed start time and return you there at the end of the day. Just share your hotel name and location when you book. If you're staying somewhere slightly outside the central area, mention it in advance so we can confirm the pickup time." },
      { question: "Are the monument entry tickets included in the price?", answer: "**Entry tickets are not included** in any of the three options — the fee covers your private guide, air-conditioned car, fuel and parking. Tickets for Amber Fort, City Palace and Jantar Mantar are paid separately on the day (typically a few hundred rupees each for foreign visitors). Your guide will help you buy them quickly at each site so you skip the confusion at the counters." },
      { question: "What's the difference between the three booking options?", answer: "The two **$60** options — \"Private Full Day Sightseeing Tour By Car with Approved Guide\" and \"Full-Day Sightseeing Tour By Car and Guide\" — cover the same 8-hour private itinerary with a car and guide. The **$70** option, \"Jaipur Full-Day Tour By Car with Guide & Buffet Lunch,\" adds a buffet lunch so you don't have to arrange a midday meal yourself. If you'd like lunch sorted for you, the $70 option is the easy choice." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or will I share it with strangers?", answer: "It is a **fully private tour** — the car and guide are yours alone, whether you're a solo traveler, a couple or a family. That means you set the pace, can linger longer at Amber Fort or skip a stop if you're tired. If you'd prefer to also explore Jaipur after dark, many guests pair this with the [Jaipur City Night Tour with Guide](/india/jaipur/jaipur-city-night-tour-with-guide)." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and is Amber Fort steep?", answer: "Expect a moderate amount of walking. **Amber Fort sits atop a hill and involves a steep ramp and steps** to reach the palace courtyards, and the stepwell at Panna Meena Ka Kund has uneven surfaces. There's plenty of pausing for photos and history along the way, and the car handles all travel between sites. Wear comfortable shoes and take it slowly and you'll be fine." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for older travelers and young children?", answer: "Yes, because it's private and car-based, you control the pace, which makes it comfortable for grandparents and kids alike. The main effort is the **climb up to Amber Fort** — older travelers can take it gently, and at Amber a jeep ride to the top is usually available for a small extra fee if the walk feels like too much. Let your guide know your group's needs and they'll adjust the day." },
      { question: "What should I wear and when is the best time to visit?", answer: "Wear light, breathable clothing, a hat and good walking shoes, and carry sunscreen and water — **Jaipur gets very hot from April to June**, often above 40°C. The most pleasant months are **October to March**. Whatever the season, starting early beats both the heat and the crowds at Amber Fort. For temple courtyards, modest clothing that covers shoulders and knees is appreciated." },
      { question: "Can I take photos at the main sites?", answer: "Absolutely — this is one of the most photogenic tours in Jaipur. The pink honeycomb façade of **Hawa Mahal** is best shot in the morning light, the **Jal Mahal** reflected on the lake is stunning, and the geometry of **Panna Meena Ka Kund** and Jantar Mantar's instruments are favourites. Some interior sections of City Palace charge a small camera fee, and your guide knows the best angles at each stop." },
      { question: "What kind of guide will I have?", answer: "You'll be paired with a **government-approved, professional guide** who is licensed and knowledgeable about Jaipur's Rajput history, architecture and astronomy. They tailor the commentary to your interests, whether that's the Hindu-Muslim design of Amber Fort or the science behind Jantar Mantar. If you specifically want a licensed guide-only experience, see [Book Official Tour Guide for Jaipur City Tour](/india/jaipur/jaipur-city-tour-with-official-guide)." },
      { question: "Is lunch provided, and are vegetarian options available?", answer: "Lunch is only included if you book the **$70 \"Guide & Buffet Lunch\" option**; the two $60 options leave you free to eat where you like. Rajasthani cuisine is very **vegetarian-friendly**, and your guide can recommend clean, authentic spots for dal baati churma or thalis. If you'd rather cook the food yourself, consider the [Jaipur Authentic Cooking Class & Dinner with Local Family](/india/jaipur/local-family-home-food-tour)." },
      { question: "Can I customise the itinerary or add stops like Nahargarh or shopping?", answer: "Yes — because the tour is private, your guide can adjust the order and add stops within the 8 hours, such as **Nahargarh Fort** for the sunset view or a quick browse through Johari or Bapu Bazaar. Do note that adding stops means less time elsewhere. If shopping is a real priority, a dedicated [Jaipur Craft & Shopping Experience](/india/jaipur/jaipur-shopping-tour) may suit you better." },
      { question: "How is this different from the half-day Jaipur tour?", answer: "The half-day version covers a shorter selection of highlights in roughly four hours, while this **full day gives you 8 hours** to properly explore Amber Fort, the Jal Mahal, Panna Meena Ka Kund and the Pink City core without rushing. If your time in Jaipur is tight, the [Govt. Approved Guide Full or Half Day City Tour](/india/jaipur/hawa-mahal-half-day-tour) is a leaner alternative, but the full day is the more complete experience." },
      { question: "What is the cancellation policy?", answer: "We offer **free cancellation** when you cancel with reasonable notice before your tour date — you'll receive a full refund. Because the guide and car are reserved privately for you, we ask that any changes to the date, time or group size are shared as early as possible so we can accommodate them. You'll find the exact deadline confirmed on your booking confirmation." },
      { question: "How do I book and confirm my tour?", answer: "Simply choose your preferred option — the two **$60** car-and-guide options or the **$70** version with buffet lunch — select your date and number of travelers, and complete the booking. You'll receive a confirmation, and we'll coordinate your **hotel pickup time** directly. If you'd like to combine Jaipur with a bigger trip, many guests add the [Jaipur to Agra Taj Mahal Day Trip](/india/jaipur/jaipur-to-agra-taj-mahal-day-trip) on a separate day." },
    ];
  }

  // --- JAIPUR: hawa-mahal-half-day-tour (auto-added 2026-07-02) ---
  if (slug === 'hawa-mahal-half-day-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What sites does this tour actually cover?", answer: "Your Govt.-approved guide leads you through Jaipur's headline landmarks: **Amer (Amber) Fort**, the stepwell at **Panna Meena ka Kund**, **Hawa Mahal**, **Jantar Mantar**, the royal cenotaphs at **Gaitor Ki Chhatriyan**, the **City Palace**, and a walk through the old Pink City bazaars. On a half-day you'll cover the essentials; the full day lets you slow down at each stop and add the local market walk." },
      { question: "What is the difference between the half-day and full-day options?", answer: "The **half-day guide** at **$123** is ideal if you have limited time and want the core icons (Amer Fort, Hawa Mahal, City Palace). The **full-day guide** at **$164** covers everything at a relaxed pace, including Jantar Mantar, Gaitor Ki Chhatriyan and the bazaar walk. If you'd rather leave the driving to us, the **guide-with-car option at $492** bundles transport for the whole day. Prefer a full sightseeing package by car? See our [Private Full Day Sightseeing Tour By Car with Approved Guide](/india/jaipur/hawa-mahal-full-day-tour)." },
      { question: "Does the price include entry tickets to the monuments?", answer: "No. The guide options here cover the **licensed guide's professional services** (and the car, if you pick that option), but **monument entry tickets are paid separately** at each site. This is standard for guide-only bookings and keeps the price low. Budget roughly 500-600 rupees for the Amer Fort composite ticket and smaller fees for Hawa Mahal, Jantar Mantar and City Palace; your guide can buy them with you so you skip the queues." },
      { question: "Is hotel pickup included?", answer: "Your guide meets you **directly at your hotel** to start the day. If you choose the **guide-with-car option ($492)**, comfortable pickup and drop-off from your hotel or the airport is included, along with tolls, parking and driver allowances. With the guide-only options you arrange your own transport, and your guide will happily coordinate a reliable car if you'd like one added." },
      { question: "How physically demanding is this tour, especially at Amer Fort?", answer: "Most of the day is easy walking, but **Amer Fort involves a steep cobbled ramp and several staircases** to reach the palace courtyards. Comfortable closed shoes make a big difference. The Pink City bazaars are flat but crowded and uneven in places. If steep climbs are a concern, your guide can pace the walk and point out where to rest." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for children and older travellers?", answer: "Yes. Because it's a **private guided tour**, the pace is entirely yours, which suits families with kids and grandparents alike. Your guide keeps the storytelling lively for younger travellers and can shorten the climb at Amer Fort for anyone who tires easily. For a gentler, car-based day with more sitting between stops, consider the [Private Full Day Sightseeing Tour By Car with Guide](/india/jaipur/jaipur-full-day-sightseeing-tour-by-car)." },
      { question: "What is the best time of day to visit these sites?", answer: "**Start early.** Reaching Amer Fort soon after opening means cooler air, softer light and far thinner crowds. Hawa Mahal's honeycomb facade glows best in the morning sun, making it a photographer's favourite. By midday the sites fill up and the heat builds, so an early start lets you enjoy the icons before it gets busy." },
      { question: "How hot does Jaipur get, and what should I wear?", answer: "Jaipur summers (April-June) can push well past 40°C, while October-March is pleasantly mild. Wear **light, breathable clothing, a hat and sunscreen**, and carry water. If you pick the car option, unlimited bottled water is included. Modest shoulder- and knee-covering dress is respectful at the City Palace and temple sites, and closed shoes help on the Amer Fort ramp." },
      { question: "Can I take photographs at the monuments?", answer: "Absolutely. **Hawa Mahal, City Palace and Jantar Mantar are among Jaipur's most photogenic spots**, and your guide knows the best angles and quiet corners for photos. A few interior areas at the City Palace charge a small camera fee, and some galleries restrict photography, which your guide will flag as you go so you never get caught out." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or shared with other travellers?", answer: "This is a fully **private guided tour** with personalized attention just for your group. You set the pace, choose how long to linger at Amer Fort or the bazaars, and can tweak the route on the day. There are no strangers tagging along and no fixed group schedule to keep up with." },
      { question: "Can I add shopping and the local bazaars to the day?", answer: "Yes. The full-day itinerary includes a **walking tour of the old Pink City and its local bazaars**, where you can browse textiles, jewellery and handicrafts around Johari and Bapu Bazaar. Your guide helps with fair pricing and steers you toward genuine workshops. If shopping is your main interest, our dedicated [Jaipur Craft & Shopping Experience with Blue Pottery and Textile Printing](/india/jaipur/jaipur-shopping-tour) goes deeper." },
      { question: "Why book a Govt.-approved guide instead of exploring on my own?", answer: "A **guide approved by the Ministry of Tourism, Govt. of India and Rajasthan Tourism** unlocks the real history, Rajput architecture and local legends you simply won't find in a guidebook or online. They know the hidden corners, the stories behind Amer Fort and City Palace, and how to skip wasted time. It turns a checklist of monuments into a day that actually makes sense." },
      { question: "What language does the guide speak?", answer: "Tours are conducted in **fluent English**, with several other languages available on request. Because the booking is private, you're paired with a certified local expert who tailors the depth and style of commentary to your interests, whether that's architecture, royal history or photography." },
      { question: "What support do I have before and during the tour?", answer: "You get **24/7 WhatsApp and phone support** both before and during the tour, so confirming your pickup time or adjusting plans on the day is easy. Applicable government service taxes are already included in the price. For a different perspective on the city, some guests pair this with the after-dark [Jaipur City Night Tour with Guide](/india/jaipur/jaipur-city-night-tour-with-guide)." },
      { question: "How do I book and can I cancel?", answer: "Booking is quick: choose your option (**half-day guide $123, full-day guide $164, or full/half day with car $492**), select your date, and you'll receive confirmation with your guide's details. We recommend booking a few days ahead in peak season (October-March). For cancellation terms and any date changes, contact us via WhatsApp and our team will help you sort it out." },
    ];
  }

