  if (slug === 'hawa-mahal-chokhi-full-day-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What exactly does this full-day Jaipur tour cover?", answer: "This tour packs Jaipur's headline sights into one day: you'll explore the hilltop **Amber Fort**, tour the **City Palace** and the astronomical **Jantar Mantar**, and make photo stops at the honeycomb-facade **Hawa Mahal**, the lake-set **Jal Mahal**, and the **Albert Hall Museum**. The day then finishes with a traditional Rajasthani dinner and live folk performances at **Chokhi Dhani**. It's a genuine highlights-plus-culture package rather than a quick drive-by." },
      { question: "How long is the tour and is dinner really included?", answer: "It's a full-day experience that runs into the evening, since Chokhi Dhani is an after-dark cultural village. Yes, the **traditional Rajasthani dinner at Chokhi Dhani is fully included**, along with entry to the village and its live performances. The single option, **Full-Day Jaipur Tour with Guide & Chokhi Dhani Dinner at $199**, covers the guide, the private vehicle, and the Chokhi Dhani experience together, so you don't pay separately for the evening." },
      { question: "Is hotel pickup included, and where do you collect me?", answer: "Yes, **pickup and drop-off from your hotel or the Jaipur airport is included** in the $199 price. You'll be met by your driver in a private air-conditioned vehicle and introduced to your English-speaking guide at the start of the day. Just share your accommodation details when you book so we can confirm an exact pickup time that leaves enough of the day for Amber Fort before the crowds build." },
      { question: "Are monument entry tickets included in the price?", answer: "The $199 option includes your guide, private A/C vehicle, all tolls, parking and driver allowances, plus **entry and dinner at Chokhi Dhani**. Entry tickets to the individual monuments such as Amber Fort, City Palace and Jantar Mantar are typically paid on the day, as ticket prices change periodically. Your guide will help you buy them quickly at each gate so you skip the confusion at the counters." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or shared with other travellers?", answer: "This is a **private tour** — the air-conditioned vehicle, driver and English-speaking guide are dedicated to your group alone. That means you set the pace at Amber Fort and the City Palace and aren't waiting on strangers. If you'd prefer a purely guide-only arrangement without the Chokhi Dhani evening, the [official Jaipur city tour with a government-approved guide](/india/jaipur/jaipur-city-tour-with-official-guide) is a leaner alternative." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and is Amber Fort a hard climb?", answer: "Expect a fair amount of walking and some climbing. **Amber Fort sits on a hill and involves a steep cobbled ramp and stairs** up to the courtyards, and the City Palace and Jantar Mantar are explored on foot. The pace is comfortable and your guide will set it to suit you, but wear sturdy shoes. If your group prefers something gentler, the [half-day Jaipur city tour](/india/jaipur/hawa-mahal-half-day-tour) trims the walking." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for kids and older travellers?", answer: "Yes. Because it's private and vehicle-based, families and older travellers can go at their own speed, rest in the A/C car between sites, and skip anything that feels too strenuous. The **Amber Fort ramp is the main physical stretch**, and it can be taken slowly. Kids usually love the puppet shows, camel rides and folk dancing at Chokhi Dhani in the evening, which makes a great end to a busy day." },
      { question: "What's the food like at Chokhi Dhani, and are vegetarian options available?", answer: "Chokhi Dhani serves a lavish **traditional Rajasthani thali** — think dal baati churma, gatte ki sabzi, bajra roti and local sweets, served in the seated village-dining style. The classic Rajasthani thali is **almost entirely vegetarian**, which suits most travellers well. Let us know in advance about any allergies or strong preferences so we can flag them, and your guide can point out the milder dishes." },
      { question: "When is the best time of day and season to do this tour?", answer: "An early start is ideal so you reach **Amber Fort before the midday heat and tour-bus crowds**. The tour is deliberately structured to end at Chokhi Dhani after sunset, when the cultural village comes alive. Season-wise, **October to March is the most comfortable**, with pleasant days for the fort. Summer (April-June) is doable in the A/C vehicle but hot on foot, so we pace outdoor stops accordingly." },
      { question: "How hot does it get, and what should I wear?", answer: "Jaipur can be very warm, especially April through June when daytime temperatures often push past 35C. Wear **light, breathable clothing, a hat and sunglasses, and comfortable closed shoes** for the Amber Fort climb. Carry water and sunscreen. For the City Palace and any temple areas, modest clothing that covers shoulders and knees is appreciated. The vehicle is air-conditioned, so you'll cool down between stops." },
      { question: "Where's the best photography on this tour?", answer: "You'll have superb photo opportunities all day. **Hawa Mahal's pink honeycomb facade is best shot in the morning light**, Jal Mahal makes a serene reflection over the water, and the Albert Hall Museum is striking at any hour. Inside Amber Fort, the Sheesh Mahal mirror work and the courtyards are highlights, and the City Palace and Jantar Mantar are wonderfully photogenic. Your guide knows the best angles at each stop." },
      { question: "Can this tour be combined with elephants, shopping or a cooking class?", answer: "This itinerary focuses on Jaipur's monuments plus the Chokhi Dhani evening, but Jaipur has plenty more if you have extra days. Animal lovers enjoy the ethical [Jaipur Elephant Village experience](/india/jaipur/elephant-village-tour-jaipur), keen shoppers can add a [blue pottery and textile-printing craft tour](/india/jaipur/jaipur-shopping-tour), and foodies often pair sightseeing with a [Jaipur cooking class and dinner with a local family](/india/jaipur/local-family-home-food-tour)." },
      { question: "Will there be time for shopping at the bazaars?", answer: "The core of the day is monuments and the Chokhi Dhani evening, but your private guide can build in a short stop at Jaipur's famous markets such as **Johari Bazaar or Bapu Bazaar** if you'd like, subject to the day's timing. It's a good chance to browse block-printed textiles, blue pottery and jewellery. Friendly bargaining is expected in the bazaars, and your guide can help you get fair prices." },
      { question: "How do I book and confirm this tour?", answer: "Booking is simple: reserve the **$199 Full-Day Jaipur Tour with Guide & Chokhi Dhani Dinner** online, then share your Jaipur hotel name and preferred date. We'll confirm your pickup time and guide details by message before the tour. Because this is a private departure operated locally, we recommend booking a few days ahead in peak season (October to March) to lock in your preferred date." },
      { question: "What is the cancellation policy?", answer: "We keep cancellation straightforward and traveller-friendly, with **free cancellation available when you cancel well ahead of your tour date**. Because this is a private tour with a dedicated guide and vehicle reserved just for you, last-minute cancellations may be subject to a charge. If your plans are uncertain, message us — we'll always try to reschedule your date rather than cancel outright where we can." },
      { question: "What if I only want the daytime sightseeing without the Chokhi Dhani dinner?", answer: "This particular tour is built around the full-day sights plus the Chokhi Dhani cultural evening as one package. If you'd rather have just the daytime monuments by private car, the [private full-day sightseeing tour by car with guide](/india/jaipur/jaipur-full-day-sightseeing-tour-by-car) covers Amber Fort, City Palace, Jantar Mantar and Hawa Mahal without the evening dinner, and can be a better fit if you have your own dinner plans." },
    ];
  }

