  if (slug === 'gateway-of-india-private-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What exactly does this 10-hour private tour cover?", answer: "You'll explore Mumbai's iconic landmarks, colonial-era architecture and bustling streets with your private guide, then take a **ferry across the Arabian Sea to Elephanta Island** to see the UNESCO-listed rock-cut cave temples. The highlight is the 5th-8th century sculptures dedicated to Lord Shiva, including the magnificent Trimurti carving. It's a full, well-paced day at **$136 per booking** covering both the city and the caves." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or will I share it with strangers?", answer: "This is a **fully private tour** for your group only. You get a private air-conditioned car with an English-speaking driver plus a dedicated English-speaking guide, so the pace, stops and timing flex around you. If you'd prefer a private city tour that swaps the caves for a deeper local experience, see our [Private Mumbai Sightseeing & Dharavi Slum Tour](/india/mumbai/gateway-of-india-sightseeing-private-tour)." },
      { question: "Are the ferry and Elephanta Caves entrance tickets included in the price?", answer: "Yes. The **$136 price includes the ferry tickets, the Elephanta Caves entrance fee, the toy train on the island, skip-the-line access at the caves, and a bottle of water on arrival**. There are no hidden ticket costs for the core itinerary, though a small island entry fee collected by local authorities and any tips are typically not covered." },
      { question: "Does the tour include hotel pickup and drop-off?", answer: "Yes, **hotel pickup and drop-off in Mumbai are included** in your private AC car. Your driver will collect you directly from your hotel lobby at the agreed morning time and return you there at the end of the day, so you don't need to arrange any separate transport." },
      { question: "How physically demanding is the visit to Elephanta Caves?", answer: "Reaching the caves involves climbing roughly **120 stone steps** from the jetty, though a toy train (included) covers the flat stretch from the pier. The paths are uneven and rocky in places. Most reasonably mobile travelers manage fine at a relaxed pace, and porters with carrying chairs are usually available on the island for a fee if the steps are too much." },
      { question: "What's the best time of day and season to do this tour?", answer: "An **early morning start is best** so you cross to the island before the midday heat and beat the largest crowds. The most comfortable months are **November to February**, when Mumbai is dry and warm. Avoid the monsoon (roughly June to September), as ferry services to Elephanta can be suspended during rough seas or heavy rain." },
      { question: "What should I wear and bring for the day?", answer: "Wear **comfortable closed shoes with grip** for the steps and uneven cave floors, plus light breathable clothing, a hat, sunglasses and sunscreen for the exposed island. Bring a little cash for snacks, tips and the small local island fee. A bottle of water is provided on arrival, but carrying extra in Mumbai's heat is wise." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for children and older travelers?", answer: "Yes, families enjoy it, especially the ferry ride and the toy train that kids love. For **older travelers, the main consideration is the climb of around 120 steps** at the caves; the pace is private and flexible, so you can rest as needed, and carrying-chair porters are available on the island. Let us know your group's needs when booking so your guide can adjust." },
      { question: "How long is the ferry ride to Elephanta Island?", answer: "The **ferry across the harbour takes roughly one hour each way** from the Gateway of India jetty. It's a scenic crossing over the Arabian Sea with views back toward the Mumbai skyline. Your guide handles the ferry tickets, so you simply board and enjoy the ride." },
      { question: "Can I take photographs at Elephanta Caves?", answer: "Absolutely, photography is allowed and the **Trimurti statue and Shiva sculptures are wonderfully photogenic**. Morning light streaming into the cave temples is ideal for the carvings. The ferry crossing and the view of the Gateway of India also make great shots, so keep your camera or phone handy throughout the day." },
      { question: "Is lunch or food included, and are vegetarian options available?", answer: "Meals are **not included** beyond the complimentary bottle of water on arrival at the island. There are simple snack stalls and cafes near the caves, and your guide can recommend good vegetarian and local spots in Mumbai for lunch. India caters extremely well to vegetarians, so dietary needs are easy to meet." },
      { question: "Do the Elephanta Caves close on any day of the week?", answer: "Yes, **Elephanta Caves are closed on Mondays**, and ferries do not run to the island that day. If your Mumbai stay falls on a Monday, we recommend an alternative such as our [Private Mumbai Sightseeing & Dharavi Slum Tour](/india/mumbai/gateway-of-india-sightseeing-private-tour), or booking this tour for another day of your trip." },
      { question: "How does skip-the-line access work at the caves?", answer: "Your booking includes **skip-the-line entry at the Elephanta Caves**, so once you've crossed on the ferry and climbed to the cave complex, your guide handles ticketing and you head straight in without queuing at the entrance. Combined with an early start, this saves considerable time on a busy day." },
      { question: "What is the cancellation policy?", answer: "We recommend booking with flexibility given that **ferry schedules to Elephanta depend on weather**. Full cancellation and refund terms are shown at checkout before you confirm; if seas are too rough for the crossing on your date, we'll work with you to reschedule or adjust the itinerary to Mumbai's city highlights." },
      { question: "Can this be combined with a Taj Mahal trip from Mumbai?", answer: "Many visitors pair a day in Mumbai with a Taj Mahal excursion. If you'd like to add the Taj, consider our [Same Day Taj Mahal Tour From Mumbai with Flight](/india/mumbai/same-day-taj-mahal-tour-from-mumbai-by-flight) for a fly-in day trip, or the [Overnight Taj Mahal Tour From Mumbai](/india/mumbai/overnight-taj-mahal-tour-from-mumbai) if you'd prefer a more relaxed two-day pace before or after your Elephanta day." },
    ];
  }

