    return [
      { question: "What exactly does this 2-day Udaipur tour cover?", answer: "Day one focuses on Udaipur city itself, taking in iconic sights like the **City Palace**, the lakes and gardens, and the Rajput heritage that gives Udaipur its 'City of Lakes' reputation. Day two is a spiritual excursion into the countryside to the historic **Eklingji and Nagda temples** just outside the city. You'll have a knowledgeable local guide and a comfortable car for both full days of sightseeing." },
      { question: "What's included in the $120 price?", answer: "The **$120 price covers the whole 2-day tour** and includes a professional tour guide for both days, a private car for all Udaipur and temple-excursion sightseeing, and all taxes, tolls, fuel and parking fees. It is a single all-inclusive option for the pair of days. **Temple donation boxes, monument entry tickets, meals and hotel stays are not included**, so budget a little extra for those." },
      { question: "Does the price include entry tickets to the City Palace and temples?", answer: "The tour package covers your **guide, car and all road costs**, but monument entrance fees such as the City Palace ticket are not included in the $120 price. Eklingji and Nagda are active places of worship, so entry is generally free, though small donations are customary. Your guide will tell you the current entry costs at each site so there are no surprises on the day." },
      { question: "Is hotel pickup and drop-off included?", answer: "Yes, because you have a **private car and driver for both full days**, your guide will collect you from and return you to your Udaipur hotel each day. When you book, please share your hotel name and preferred start time so pickup can be arranged smoothly. Most guests based in the old city or near Lake Pichola find pickup very convenient." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or a shared group tour?", answer: "This is a **private guided tour** with your own dedicated guide and car for the full two days, so the pace is set entirely by you and your party. There are no strangers joining and no fixed group timetable. If you'd prefer a single-day city experience instead, the [Udaipur private full-day sightseeing tour](/india/udaipur/lake-pichola-full-day-tour) is a good shorter alternative." },
      { question: "How far are Eklingji and Nagda from Udaipur, and how long is the drive?", answer: "**Eklingji and Nagda sit around 22 km north of Udaipur**, roughly a 45-minute drive each way through the Aravalli countryside. Since the two temples are close together, you can comfortably visit both in a half to full day on day two. The scenic drive is part of the experience, and because the car is private you can stop for photos along the way." },
      { question: "What should I wear, especially for the temples?", answer: "Eklingji is a **living Hindu temple**, so modest dress is essential, shoulders and knees covered for everyone, and you'll remove your shoes before entering. Comfortable walking shoes are ideal for uneven temple courtyards and City Palace ramps. In the warmer months bring light, breathable cotton, a hat and sunscreen, and a small shawl for the temples." },
      { question: "When is the best time of year to do this tour?", answer: "**October to March is the most comfortable season** in Udaipur, with warm days and cool evenings that are perfect for two full days of sightseeing. April to June can be very hot, often above 40C, so an earlier morning start helps. The monsoon months of July to September bring lush green hills and fuller lakes, which many travellers love for photography." },
      { question: "Is there much walking or climbing involved?", answer: "There's a **moderate amount of walking** across City Palace courtyards and the temple complexes, along with some steps and uneven stone underfoot. Eklingji's ancient layout and Nagda's ruins involve gentle exploration rather than steep climbs. The private car reduces distances between sites, so with sensible shoes most reasonably mobile travellers manage comfortably at their own pace." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for children and older travellers?", answer: "Yes, the **private format makes it very flexible** for families and older guests, since you can rest in the car, shorten stops or skip anything tiring. The mix of palaces, lakes and temples keeps children interested, though very young ones may find two full days long. Let your guide know about any mobility needs so the route can be paced gently." },
      { question: "Where can we eat, and are vegetarian options available?", answer: "Meals aren't included, but your guide is happy to recommend and stop at good local restaurants between sightseeing, from lakeside rooftop spots to authentic Rajasthani thali. **Vegetarian food is abundant everywhere in Udaipur**, and the temple town area around Eklingji is largely vegetarian and often alcohol-free. Just tell your guide your preferences or any dietary needs and they'll steer you well." },
      { question: "Can I take photographs at the sights?", answer: "Photography is welcome across most of Udaipur's palaces, gardens and lakes, and the guide will point out the best viewpoints. **Note that Eklingji temple strictly prohibits photography and phones inside the main shrine**, as it is an active place of worship, though the surrounding architecture and Nagda's ruins are photogenic. Some City Palace areas may charge a small camera fee." },
      { question: "What sights might we see beyond the City Palace on day one?", answer: "Alongside the **grand City Palace**, day one typically weaves in Udaipur's celebrated lakes, ornamental gardens and heritage streets that showcase its Rajput history. Your private guide tailors the exact route to your interests and pace. If you want to add a boat perspective of Lake Pichola or dedicate more time to the old city, discuss it with your guide at the start of the day." },
      { question: "What is the cancellation policy and how do I confirm my booking?", answer: "Once you book, you'll receive a **confirmation with your guide's details and pickup arrangements**. We recommend confirming your hotel and preferred start time in advance so both days run smoothly. For the current cancellation and refund terms, check the booking page at checkout or contact us, as flexible options are usually available for private tours booked ahead." },
      { question: "Can I combine this with other day trips from Udaipur?", answer: "Absolutely, many guests pair this city-and-temple tour with longer excursions into Rajasthan. Popular add-ons include the [Kumbhalgarh and Ranakpur day round trip](/india/udaipur/ranakpur-jain-temple-spiritual-tour) for its fort and marble Jain temples, or a [Chittorgarh Fort day trip by car](/india/udaipur/chittorgarh-fort-full-day-tour). If you'd rather keep things within the city, the [full-day sightseeing tour with an official guide](/india/udaipur/city-palace-full-day-tour) makes a great companion day." },
    ];
