  if (slug === 'jaisalmer-fort-half-day-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What exactly will I see on this half-day Jaisalmer tour?", answer: "This 6-hour guided tour covers Jaisalmer's essential landmarks by private AC car. You'll explore the golden sandstone **Jaisalmer Fort**, the intricately carved **Patwon Ki Haveli** and **Nathmal Ki Haveli**, **Badal Mahal**, the serene **Gadisar Lake**, the elegant cenotaphs at **Vyas Chhatri**, **Mandir Palace**, and the royal gardens near **Amar Sagar**, including Amar Singh Palace and an old Shiva temple. Your local guide ties each stop to the city's history and Rajput heritage." },
      { question: "Is hotel pickup included, and where does the tour start?", answer: "Yes, the tour is designed to begin from your hotel or guesthouse within Jaisalmer, since you travel in a **private AC car** with your own guide and driver. Just share your accommodation details when you book so we can confirm the pickup point. If you're staying inside the fort walls where vehicles can't reach, we'll arrange a convenient meeting point nearby." },
      { question: "Does the price of $90 include entry tickets to the monuments?", answer: "The **$90 price** covers your private car, driver, official guide, water and snacks. Small **entry fees at sites like Patwon Ki Haveli, Gadisar Lake and any camera charges** are typically paid directly on-site and are modest (a few dollars total). We recommend carrying a little cash in rupees for these tickets and for any optional treats along the way." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and is the tour physically demanding?", answer: "The tour is car-based, so drives between sites are comfortable, but exploring **Jaisalmer Fort and the havelis does involve walking on uneven cobblestones, narrow lanes and some stairs**. The fort sits on a hill, so there's a gentle climb to reach and move around it. It's manageable at a relaxed pace, but wear sturdy, closed shoes and let your guide know if you'd prefer to slow down." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for young children and older travelers?", answer: "Yes, it works well for families and seniors because most travel is by private car and the guide sets the pace to suit you. Do keep in mind the **cobblestone lanes and steps inside the fort and havelis** can be tiring for very young children or those with mobility issues. The car is always close by for rest breaks, and the driver can wait while you explore at your own speed." },
      { question: "What is the best time of day to take this tour?", answer: "An **early morning start (around 8-9 am)** is ideal, especially from March to June, so you finish before the fierce midday heat and enjoy softer light for photos at the fort and Gadisar Lake. Morning also means fewer crowds inside Patwon Ki Haveli. In the cooler winter months an afternoon start works beautifully too, with golden light on the sandstone near sunset." },
      { question: "What should I wear and bring for the day?", answer: "Jaisalmer sits in the Thar Desert, so dress for **strong sun and dry heat**: light, breathable clothing, a hat, sunglasses and sunscreen. Comfortable closed walking shoes are essential for the fort's uneven stone. Bring a little cash in rupees for entry tickets, and although water is provided, an extra bottle never hurts. In winter mornings a light layer is useful as it can be cool." },
      { question: "What food and refreshments are included?", answer: "Your tour includes **water and snacks**, and your guide will point you toward authentic local delicacies to taste as you explore the old city. This is a great chance to try Rajasthani specialties recommended by someone who knows the best spots. Full meals aren't included, but the guide is happy to suggest excellent nearby restaurants if you'd like to add lunch before or after." },
      { question: "Can you cater to vegetarian or specific dietary needs?", answer: "Absolutely. Rajasthani cuisine is famously **vegetarian-friendly**, so if you'd like to sample local snacks or dishes during the tour, your guide can steer you toward vegetarian, vegan or Jain-friendly options. Let us know about any allergies or dietary restrictions in advance and the guide will make suitable recommendations at each food stop." },
      { question: "Is this tour private or shared with other travelers?", answer: "This is a fully **private tour**: just your group, your own official guide and a private AC car with driver. That means the itinerary flexes to your interests, you can linger longer at a haveli or the fort, and there's no waiting on strangers. It's a personal, unhurried way to see Jaisalmer's highlights in a single half-day." },
      { question: "How good is the photography on this tour?", answer: "Exceptional. Jaisalmer is called the **Golden City** for good reason, and this tour hits its most photogenic spots: the honey-colored fort ramparts, the ornate stone latticework of Patwon Ki Haveli and Nathmal Ki Haveli, reflections on Gadisar Lake, and the elegant chhatris at Vyas Chhatri. Note that some interiors charge a small camera fee, and your guide knows the best angles and light for each site." },
      { question: "How does this compare to a walking tour of Jaisalmer?", answer: "This tour covers more ground by car, reaching sites like Amar Sagar and Vyas Chhatri that are outside the old city core. If you'd rather explore the fort's lanes and living heritage on foot at a slower rhythm, consider the [Jaisalmer Heritage Walk](/india/jaisalmer/jaisalmer-fort-walking-tour) or the [Jaisalmer Heritage Walking Tour With Professional Guide](/india/jaisalmer/jaisalmer-fort-heritage-walking-tour). Many travelers pair a walking tour with this car-based highlights tour across two days." },
      { question: "Can I add a desert safari or camel experience to my trip?", answer: "This particular tour focuses on the city's forts, havelis and lakes rather than the dunes. If you want the classic Thar Desert experience, we recommend booking the separate [Jeep Safari, Camel Ride, Dinner and Folk Dance](/india/jaisalmer/jaisalmer-fort-guided-tour) for the late afternoon and evening. Doing the highlights tour in the morning and the desert safari at sunset makes for a perfect full day in Jaisalmer." },
      { question: "Do I need a licensed guide, and is the guide knowledgeable?", answer: "Your guide is a **highly trained, friendly official tour guide** who shares the history, beliefs and local significance behind each monument. If you specifically want to book a certified guide for the fort itself, you can also look at the [licensed and certified Jaisalmer Fort guide](/india/jaisalmer/jaisalmer-fort-certified-guided-tour) option. On this tour, the guide's local insight and conversations are one of the biggest highlights." },
      { question: "How do I book, and what is the cancellation policy?", answer: "Booking is simple: reserve online, share your hotel and preferred start time, and you'll receive confirmation of your pickup details. We recommend booking a day or two ahead so we can secure your private car and guide. For cancellations, please contact us as early as possible; our team will confirm the exact terms and any free-cancellation window when you book so there are no surprises." },
    ];
  }

