  if (slug === 'koh-larn-coral-island-guided-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What is included in the $10 Pattaya Coral Island tour price?", answer: "The **$10 per person** rate covers your **hotel pickup and drop-off** within Pattaya, the **speedboat transfer** out to Koh Larn and back, and an **Indian lunch** on the day. Water sports like parasailing, jet skiing and sea walking are exciting add-ons paid separately on the island, so you only pay for the activities you actually want to try." },
      { question: "How does hotel pickup work and which areas are covered?", answer: "A driver collects you directly from your hotel lobby in the **Pattaya area**, so there's no need to find your own way to the pier. You'll typically be picked up in the morning to make the most of the 6-hour day. When you book, just share your hotel name and room details so the team can confirm your exact pickup time the evening before." },
      { question: "How long is the tour and what does the day look like?", answer: "The full experience runs about **6 hours** door to door, including transfers. After hotel pickup you'll board a **speedboat for the roughly 15-minute crossing** to Koh Larn, spend the bulk of the day on the beaches and in the water, break for your included Indian lunch, then speed back to the mainland. It's an efficient day trip that packs in a lot without an overnight stay." },
      { question: "Is this a guided group tour or a private trip?", answer: "This is a **guided shared tour**, so you'll be with a small group and a guide who handles the boat logistics, timings and directing you to the water-sports desks and lunch. It's a sociable, easygoing format that's ideal for solo travellers, couples and families who want someone to take care of the arrangements while they relax." },
      { question: "What is sea walking and do I need to know how to swim?", answer: "Sea walking is a signature Koh Larn highlight where you wear a specialised **\"fishbowl\" helmet** that keeps your head dry while you walk along the seabed and see fish up close. Because the helmet supplies air and you stay upright on the bottom, **you don't need to be a strong swimmer**, which makes it popular even with nervous first-timers. It's an optional paid activity on the island." },
      { question: "Tell me about the parasailing — is it safe?", answer: "Parasailing here is the classic experience where you're **towed behind a speedboat** and lifted high above the turquoise water for sweeping views back toward Pattaya. Operators use a harness and an experienced boat crew, and most rides are tandem or accompanied, so it's suitable for beginners. It's an optional beachside thrill paid on the day rather than being part of the base price." },
      { question: "Which beaches will we visit on Koh Larn?", answer: "Most trips base themselves at the island's popular sandy stretches such as **Tawaen Beach**, the busiest and best set up for water sports, and quieter spots like **Tien Beach** for relaxed sunbathing. The powdery white sand and clear water are exactly the tropical scenery travellers picture, all just seven kilometres off the Pattaya coast." },
      { question: "Is the tour suitable for children and older travellers?", answer: "Yes. The relaxed beach time, short speedboat crossing and included lunch make it comfortable for **families with kids and for older travellers** who simply want to enjoy the sand and views. The adrenaline activities are all optional, so younger children or those who prefer to stay dry can sunbathe and paddle while others try parasailing or jet skiing." },
      { question: "I'm vegetarian — will the Indian lunch suit me?", answer: "Indian cuisine is naturally rich in **vegetarian dishes**, so there are usually good meat-free options as part of the included lunch. If you have specific dietary needs such as vegan, Jain, halal or allergies, let the team know when you book so they can note it in advance and make sure you're well looked after on the island." },
      { question: "What should I wear and bring for the day?", answer: "Wear your **swimwear under light clothing**, and bring a towel, sunscreen, sunglasses and a hat — Pattaya's tropical sun is strong out on the open beaches. Water shoes or sandals help on the sand and boat, and a **dry bag or waterproof pouch** is smart for protecting your phone during the speedboat ride and water sports." },
      { question: "When is the best time of year to do this trip?", answer: "Koh Larn is a great day trip year-round, but the **cool, dry season from November to February** brings the calmest seas and clearest water, which is ideal for sea walking and beach time. The March–May months are hotter, while the mid-year monsoon can bring afternoon showers, though mornings often stay bright and the sheltered bays remain enjoyable." },
      { question: "Will I have time and good spots for photos?", answer: "Absolutely — the white sand, turquoise water and views back toward the Pattaya skyline are wonderfully photogenic. **Parasailing gives you dramatic aerial shots**, and the beaches are perfect for relaxed photos. Bring a waterproof case or an action camera if you want to capture the sea walking and speedboat moments without risking your phone." },
      { question: "How physically demanding is the tour?", answer: "The day is **low to moderate in effort**. There's some walking on soft sand and stepping on and off the speedboat, which can be a little bumpy on choppy days, but nothing strenuous. The optional water sports vary in intensity — sea walking is gentle, while jet skiing and parasailing are more active — so you can pace the day to suit your comfort level." },
      { question: "Are the optional water sports expensive on the island?", answer: "Because parasailing, jet skiing and sea walking are **paid separately on Koh Larn**, prices are set by the local operators at the beach rather than included in the $10 base fare. It's wise to carry some **Thai baht in cash** for these activities, drinks and any extras, and to agree the price before you start each activity." },
      { question: "What is the cancellation policy and how do I confirm my booking?", answer: "Once you book online you'll receive a **confirmation with your pickup details**, and the team will reconfirm your exact hotel pickup time the day before. For cancellations, please contact us as early as possible — flexible terms typically apply when you cancel well in advance. If sea conditions ever make the speedboat crossing unsafe, the trip may be rescheduled for your safety." },
      { question: "Is Koh Larn a good alternative to travelling further south in Thailand?", answer: "Very much so. Koh Larn delivers the **turquoise water and powdery white sand** most people associate with southern islands like Phuket or Krabi, but it's only about seven kilometres off Pattaya and reached in minutes by speedboat. That makes it the perfect \"best of both worlds\" day out when you want tropical island scenery without long travel times." },
    ];
  }

  // --- REMAINING: hazrat-nizamuddin-railway-station-delhi-express-tour (auto-added 2026-07-02) ---
  if (slug === 'hazrat-nizamuddin-railway-station-delhi-express-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "Which train will I actually travel on for this Delhi-Agra day trip?", answer: "You'll travel on one of India's two fastest trains, the **Gatimaan Express** or the **Vande Bharat Express**, in modern air-conditioned **CC (Chair Car) Class**. Both cover the Delhi-Agra route in roughly **1.5 to 2 hours**, so you spend the day exploring rather than sitting in Delhi traffic. The exact train is assigned based on the day's schedule and confirmed availability." },
      { question: "Are the train tickets confirmed, or am I booking a waitlist?", answer: "Your booking includes **round-trip confirmed CC Class tickets** on the Gatimaan or Vande Bharat, not a waitlist. Because these fast trains sell out quickly, we lock in your seats once your booking is finalised. This is one of the main advantages of a train day trip over the road journey you'd take on the [same-day trip by car](/india/delhi/private-taj-mahal-tour-from-delhi)." },
      { question: "What's included in the $68 price, and what costs extra?", answer: "The **$68** fare covers your round-trip CC Class train tickets, a local guide in Agra, a private car for the city tour, pickup and drop at Agra Cantt railway station, the golf cart to the Taj Mahal, and water bottles. **Monument entrance fees and lunch are only included if you book those add-on options.** If you'd prefer everything bundled upfront, the [private day tour with a 5-star lunch](/india/delhi/delhi-agra-private-tour) may suit you better." },
      { question: "Which monuments does the tour cover in Agra?", answer: "You'll visit the two icons of Agra: the **Taj Mahal**, the white-marble mausoleum Shah Jahan built for Mumtaz Mahal, and the **Agra Fort**, the red-sandstone residence of the Mughal emperors. Your local guide accompanies you through both, sharing the history behind the architecture. It's a focused itinerary designed to fit comfortably into the same-day train window." },
      { question: "Where and when does the train depart from in Delhi?", answer: "Both the Gatimaan and Vande Bharat depart early in the morning from Delhi (the Gatimaan runs from Hazrat Nizamuddin station), which is why this is a same-day return. Please arrive at the station well ahead of departure with your ID and ticket ready. You'll return to Delhi in the evening on the same fast-train service after your Agra sightseeing." },
      { question: "Does this tour include hotel pickup, or do I meet at the station?", answer: "This is a **train-based tour**, so you make your own way to the Delhi departure station for the morning service; hotel transfers in Delhi are not part of the package. Once you reach **Agra Cantt station**, everything is handled for you: your car and guide meet you and drop you back for the return train. If you'd rather be collected from your Delhi hotel door-to-door, consider the [private day tour by car](/india/delhi/private-taj-mahal-agra-day-tour-from-delhi)." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and is the tour physically demanding?", answer: "There's a fair amount of **walking on marble and uneven historic stone**, plus some gentle ramps and steps at Agra Fort. To ease the approach to the Taj, a **golf cart** is included from the parking area to the entrance gate. Most reasonably mobile travellers manage comfortably, but wear cushioned walking shoes and take your time in the heat." },
      { question: "Is this trip suitable for children and older travellers?", answer: "Yes. The comfortable air-conditioned train, the included golf cart to the Taj, and the private car between sights make this an easy option for families and seniors compared with a long road trip. The pace is steady rather than rushed, and your guide can adjust to slower walkers. Just factor in the **early morning start**, which younger children may find tiring." },
      { question: "Can I get vegetarian or special meals, and what does lunch involve?", answer: "Lunch is an optional add-on served at a **five-star hotel** in Agra, and Indian five-star buffets always feature an extensive **vegetarian selection** alongside other cuisines, so vegetarians, vegans and most dietary needs are well catered for. If you don't book the lunch option, you're free to arrange your own meal. Onboard, complimentary refreshments are typically served on the Gatimaan and Vande Bharat." },
      { question: "When is the best time of year and time of day to visit the Taj Mahal on this tour?", answer: "The most pleasant months are **October to March**, when Delhi and Agra are cool and clear. April to June brings intense heat (often 40C+), and July to September is the humid monsoon. Because you arrive mid-morning, the marble can be bright and hot underfoot in summer, so a **sunrise-focused tour** like the [sunrise Taj Mahal tour](/india/delhi/sunrise-taj-mahal-tour-delhi-all-inclusive) is worth considering if you want softer light and cooler temperatures." },
      { question: "What should I wear and bring for the day?", answer: "Wear light, breathable, **modest clothing** (shoulders and knees covered is respectful at the monuments), comfortable walking shoes, sunglasses and a hat. Bring sunscreen, your **photo ID for the train**, and some cash for personal extras. Water bottles are provided, but you may want to carry a little more in summer." },
      { question: "Can I take photos at the Taj Mahal and Agra Fort?", answer: "Absolutely, both sites are wonderfully photogenic. **Photography is permitted in the gardens and grounds**, though it's restricted inside the main mausoleum chamber of the Taj, and tripods generally aren't allowed. Your guide knows the classic viewpoints for that perfect reflection shot and can help with your photos." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or a shared group?", answer: "The Agra portion is run with a **private car and a dedicated local guide** for your sightseeing, while the train journey itself is in a shared CC Class coach with other passengers. It's a nice balance of efficient rail travel and personal on-the-ground service. For a fully private experience end to end, the [luxury car day trip](/india/delhi/taj-mahal-agra-day-trip-luxury-car) is an alternative." },
      { question: "How long is the total day, and is it rushed?", answer: "Plan for a **full day**, roughly from the early-morning train out of Delhi to an evening return, with about 1.5-2 hours each way on the rails. That leaves a solid block for the Taj Mahal and Agra Fort at a comfortable pace. It's efficient rather than leisurely, but the fast train means far less time lost than a road day trip." },
      { question: "Is the train and Agra experience safe for solo and first-time travellers?", answer: "Yes. The Gatimaan and Vande Bharat are modern, secure, air-conditioned services, and you're met and escorted throughout Agra by your guide and driver, so you're never navigating alone. Around busy monuments you may encounter souvenir sellers, but your guide helps you sidestep the touts. It's one of the most stress-free ways for first-timers to see the Taj." },
      { question: "How do I book, and what's the cancellation policy?", answer: "Simply reserve online and you'll receive confirmation once your **confirmed CC Class train seats** are secured. Because fast-train tickets are booked in your name and sell out early, we recommend booking well ahead, especially in peak season (October-March). Please review the cancellation terms at checkout before you confirm, and reach out with any special requests such as adding the lunch or entrance-fee options." },
    ];
  }

  // --- REMAINING: taj-mahal-sunrise-tour-tour (auto-added 2026-07-02) ---
  if (slug === 'taj-mahal-sunrise-tour-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "Where does this tour start, and does it include pickup from my Delhi hotel?", answer: "Yes, **hotel or airport pickup and drop-off in Delhi are included**, and the driver can also collect you from Noida or Gurugram. Because the drive to Agra is 200–240 km via the Yamuna Expressway (3–4 hours each way), pickups are early — anywhere between **2:30 a.m. and 10:00 a.m.** depending on whether you choose the sunrise or standard daytime start. Share your exact hotel address when booking so the driver can plan the route." },
      { question: "What's the difference between the two booking options and their prices?", answer: "The standard **Taj Mahal Sunrise/Day tour by Car from Delhi is $160**, and both options run the full **12 hours** with a private AC car, driver, live guide, all monument entrance tickets and lunch. The **All Inclusive option at $1,952** is our top-tier package for larger private groups or fully premium arrangements. Both include the same core sightseeing — Taj Mahal, Agra Fort and the Baby Taj — so most solo travellers and couples choose the $160 option." },
      { question: "Are the Taj Mahal and monument entry tickets included, or do I pay at the gate?", answer: "**All monument entrance tickets are included** in both options — that covers the Taj Mahal, Agra Fort and Itimad-ud-Daulah (the Baby Taj). You won't need to queue separately or pay extra at any gate. If you'd rather just secure admission without transport, see the [Taj Mahal Entry Ticket 2026 – Skip-the-Line Official Admission](/india/agra/taj-mahal-entry-ticket) instead." },
      { question: "Should I choose the sunrise start or the regular daytime departure?", answer: "Sunrise is magical — the white marble shifts from soft pink to gold and the crowds are thinnest, but it means a **pickup around 2:30–3:00 a.m.** to reach Agra by first light. The daytime start is gentler if you're not an early riser, though the Taj is busier and warmer by mid-morning. If sunrise is your priority, you might also compare our dedicated [Skip-The-Line Taj Mahal Sunrise Tour With Approved Tour Guide](/india/agra/taj-mahal-sunrise-tour)." },
      { question: "How long do I actually get at the Taj Mahal itself?", answer: "You'll have roughly **2–3 hours at the Taj Mahal**, which is plenty of time for the main mausoleum, the gardens and unhurried photos. The rest of the 12 hours covers the drive, Agra Fort, the Baby Taj, lunch and your return to Delhi. Your guide paces the day so nothing feels rushed while still getting you back the same evening." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or shared with other travellers?", answer: "This is a **fully private tour** — the air-conditioned car, driver and live guide are dedicated to your party alone, so you control the pace and can linger where you like. For an even more premium private experience, some guests prefer the [Private Royal Luxury Taj Mahal Tour](/india/agra/taj-mahal-royal-private-tour)." },
      { question: "What's included for food, and can you cater to vegetarians?", answer: "**Lunch at a restaurant is included**, along with complimentary bottled water throughout the journey. Agra has excellent vegetarian, vegan and Jain-friendly options, so let your guide know your dietary needs and they'll steer the choice of restaurant. If you specifically want a higher-end meal, the [Taj Mahal & Agra Private Day Tour With 5* Lunch](/india/agra/taj-mahal-agra-private-day-tour-with-lunch) is worth a look." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and is the tour suitable for older travellers?", answer: "Expect a fair amount of walking on **marble, uneven stone and some steps**, especially inside Agra Fort's ramps and the Taj complex. It's very manageable at a relaxed pace, and because the car drops you close to each entrance, older travellers usually cope well. Wheelchairs are permitted at the Taj Mahal, so mention any mobility needs in advance and your guide will plan accordingly." },
      { question: "Is this tour a good choice for families with children?", answer: "Absolutely — the private car means you set the rhythm, take breaks and manage nap times or snacks freely. Kids generally love the scale of Agra Fort and the story of the Taj Mahal, and the included water and lunch keep everyone comfortable. Just be aware the **early sunrise start can be tiring for young children**, so families sometimes prefer the standard daytime departure." },
      { question: "What should I wear and expect from the weather in Agra?", answer: "Agra is **hot most of the year**, with April–June often exceeding 40°C, so light breathable clothing, a hat and sunscreen are essential; November–February is pleasantly cool and the most comfortable season to visit. As monuments are places of worship and heritage, modest clothing covering shoulders and knees is respectful. You'll also remove or cover your shoes near the main Taj mausoleum, so slip-on footwear is handy." },
      { question: "Can I take photographs, and where are cameras restricted?", answer: "Photography is welcome across the grounds of the Taj Mahal, Agra Fort and the Baby Taj, and sunrise light is spectacular for shots. Note that **photography is not allowed inside the main mausoleum chamber** of the Taj. If capturing images is your main goal, consider the dedicated [Taj Mahal Photography Tour with a Professional Guide](/india/agra/taj-mahal-photography-tour)." },
      { question: "Is the Baby Taj (Itimad-ud-Daulah) really worth including?", answer: "Yes — the **Itimad-ud-Daulah is a jewel-box of inlaid marble** that predates the Taj Mahal and directly inspired it, yet sees far fewer visitors. It's a peaceful, beautifully detailed stop and a highlight for anyone interested in Mughal craftsmanship. Having your guide explain its history makes the finer stonework come alive in a way that's easy to miss on your own." },
      { question: "Is the long drive from Delhi safe and comfortable?", answer: "Very — you travel in a **private, air-conditioned car with an experienced professional driver** along the well-maintained Yamuna Expressway, with driver allowances, parking, tolls and taxes all included. The vehicle is yours for the day, so you can stop for a rest or refreshments as needed. The 3–4 hour each-way journey is smooth, and the AC is a real relief in Agra's heat." },
      { question: "Do I need to book in advance, and how is the tour confirmed?", answer: "We recommend booking a few days ahead so we can arrange your guide, tickets and pickup time — especially for a sunrise start. Once booked, you'll receive **confirmation with your pickup details and driver contact** so you know exactly when to be ready. Remember the Taj Mahal is **closed on Fridays**, so if your date lands on a Friday, ask us about the [Agra Friday Special Tour alternative](/india/agra/agra-friday-tour-taj-closed-alternative)." },
      { question: "What is the cancellation policy if my plans change?", answer: "Plans change, and we aim to keep things flexible — most bookings can be cancelled or rescheduled with reasonable notice before your tour date. Because this is a private tour with a dedicated car, guide and pre-booked tickets, we ask you to notify us as early as possible so we can adjust. Reach out to our team directly and we'll confirm the exact terms that apply to your booking date." },
    ];
  }

