  if (slug === 'taj-mahal-mehtab-guided-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "Which places does this 6-hour tour actually cover?", answer: "You'll visit four of Agra's Mughal highlights in one day: the **Taj Mahal**, the sprawling **Agra Fort**, the elegant **Baby Taj (Itmad-ud-Daulah)**, and finally **Mehtab Bagh** for a sunset view across the river to the back of the Taj. It's a well-rounded loop that pairs the famous icons with the quieter, lesser-visited gems. If you only want the two headline monuments, the [Taj Mahal & Agra Fort Guided Tour](/india/agra/taj-mahal-agra-fort-guided-tour) is a shorter alternative." },
      { question: "Do all the options include skip-the-line entry tickets?", answer: "No — read the option name carefully before booking. The **$15 base option** and the **$25 Car & Guide option** are guide/transport only; you pay your own entrance fees at each monument. Only the **$60 (Guide, Car & Entrance Tickets)** and **$70 (Guide, Private Car, Entrance Fees & Meal)** options include the Taj Mahal skip-the-line ticket and other admissions. If you just want the ticket by itself, see the [Taj Mahal Entry Ticket](/india/agra/taj-mahal-entry-ticket) page." },
      { question: "What's the difference between the $60 and $70 options?", answer: "Both give you the guide, a **private car**, and all entrance fees (Taj Mahal, Agra Fort, Baby Taj, Mehtab Bagh). The **$70 option adds a 5-star restaurant meal** — breakfast or lunch depending on your pickup time. If you'd rather choose and pay for your own local eatery, the $60 option keeps things flexible and a little cheaper." },
      { question: "Does the tour include hotel pickup and drop-off?", answer: "Pickup and drop are included **only on the options with a car** — the $25, $60, and $70 tiers. We can collect you from **wherever you're staying in Agra, or from the airport**, and drop you back afterwards. On the $15 guide-only option you meet your guide at the Taj Mahal and arrange your own transport between sites." },
      { question: "Is the meal vegetarian-friendly, and can dietary needs be accommodated?", answer: "Yes. The 5-star breakfast or lunch (included on the **$70 option**) is at a proper restaurant, and Agra's dining scene is very **vegetarian-friendly** — Jain, vegan, and no-onion-garlic requests are all easy to arrange. Just mention any allergies or preferences to your guide at the start. On other options you pick your own spot, so you're free to choose based on your diet." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and is it suitable for older travellers?", answer: "Expect a **fair amount of walking on uneven stone**, especially at Agra Fort, which has ramps, cobbles, and some steps. The Taj Mahal grounds are large but mostly flat, and a **golf cart is included** to cover the distance from the gate to the mausoleum. Older travellers manage the tour comfortably at a relaxed pace — just wear supportive shoes and tell your guide if you'd like to slow down." },
      { question: "Why does the tour visit Mehtab Bagh at the end?", answer: "**Mehtab Bagh** sits directly across the Yamuna River from the Taj Mahal, so it's the classic spot to watch the marble glow at **sunset** from behind. Ending here means you see the Taj from two completely different perspectives in one day — up close in the morning and framed by garden and river light in the evening. It's calm, uncrowded, and a lovely way to wrap up." },
      { question: "Is the Taj Mahal closed on any day I should avoid?", answer: "Yes — the **Taj Mahal is closed every Friday** for prayers, so this tour doesn't run that day. Agra Fort, Baby Taj, and Mehtab Bagh stay open, so if you're in town on a Friday consider the [Agra Friday Special Tour](/india/agra/agra-friday-tour-taj-closed-alternative) instead, which covers the fort, Baby Taj, and Mehtab Bagh sunset." },
      { question: "What should I wear and when is the best season to go?", answer: "Dress modestly and comfortably, with **shoes you can walk in** (shoe covers for the Taj marble are provided). October to March brings pleasant, cooler days and is ideal; April to June gets very hot, so an earlier pickup and lots of water help. A hat and sunscreen are smart year-round, and a light layer is handy for the cooler winter mornings and Mehtab Bagh sunsets." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or shared with strangers?", answer: "The car options ($25, $60, $70) are run as **private experiences** — it's just you, your group, and your guide, with a private vehicle. That means you set the pace and can linger where you like. For a fully upgraded private day with extra polish, take a look at the [Private Royal Luxury Taj Mahal Tour](/india/agra/taj-mahal-royal-private-tour)." },
      { question: "Can I take photos, and does the guide help with them?", answer: "Absolutely — the Taj Mahal, Baby Taj's inlay work, and the Mehtab Bagh sunset are all wonderfully photogenic, and your guide knows the best angles and quieter moments to shoot. Note that **tripods aren't allowed inside the Taj**, and photography is restricted inside the main mausoleum chamber. If photos are your main goal, the dedicated [Taj Mahal Photography Tour](/india/agra/taj-mahal-photography-tour) goes deeper." },
      { question: "Is the tour suitable for kids?", answer: "Yes, families are very welcome. The pace is flexible, the included **golf cart** keeps little legs from tiring at the Taj, and the guide can keep the history lively and age-appropriate. Bring water (a bottle is included), sun protection, and snacks for younger children, since the day runs around six hours across several sites." },
      { question: "What time does the tour start?", answer: "Start time is flexible and tied to your pickup — an **earlier start pairs with breakfast**, a later one with lunch (on the meal-inclusive $70 option). Mornings are cooler and the Taj is at its most atmospheric, and starting earlier gives you a relaxed run through all four sites finishing at Mehtab Bagh for sunset. If you specifically want the dawn light, consider the [Taj Mahal Sunrise Tour](/india/agra/taj-mahal-sunrise-tour)." },
      { question: "How does the skip-the-line entry actually work?", answer: "On the ticket-inclusive options, your guide handles the pre-booked admission so you get **express entry at the Taj Mahal and Agra Fort** without queuing at the counter. There can still be a short security screening line at peak times, but you'll bypass the main ticket queues, which saves a lot of time on busy mornings." },
      { question: "How do I book and confirm, and what's the cancellation policy?", answer: "Book online by choosing your option ($15 to $70) and pickup details; you'll receive confirmation with your guide's contact so you can coordinate the exact start time. We recommend **free cancellation up to 24 hours** before the tour for a full refund — check the policy shown at checkout for your date. Reach out anytime before the day if your plans or hotel change." },
    ];
  }

  // --- REMAINING: phuket-jet-ski-tour-island-hopping-patong-beach (auto-added 2026-07-02) ---
  if (slug === 'phuket-jet-ski-tour-island-hopping-patong-beach') {
    return [
      { question: "What's the difference between the guided island hopping tour and the jet ski rental options?", answer: "The **Island Hopping Jet Ski Tour (Guided, 3 Hours) — $259** is a full escorted ride from Patong Beach past Paradise, Freedom, Karon and Kata beaches, around Laem Krating headland, all the way to **Promthep Cape** with a swimming stop, drinking water and a professional guide. The rentals — from **$69 for a solo 30-minute ride** — are self-drive laps in the water off Patong Beach with no guide or set route. Choose the guided tour if you want the scenery and distance; choose a rental if you just want a quick adrenaline hit." },
      { question: "How much does each option cost and how long does it last?", answer: "There are four options: **Island Hopping Guided Tour — $259 for 3 hours**, **Solo Jet Ski Rental 30 minutes — $69**, **Solo Jet Ski Rental 60 minutes — $139**, and **Duo Jet Ski Rental 30 minutes for 2 riders — $105**. Every option includes a life jacket, a safety briefing and a Yamaha WaveRunner; only the guided tour adds a professional guide, drinking water and the Promthep Cape swimming stop." },
      { question: "Do I need a licence or previous experience to drive the jet ski?", answer: "No licence or prior experience is required — the WaveRunners are automatic and beginner-friendly. Every option starts with a **hands-on safety briefing** covering throttle, steering and stopping before you head out. On the guided tour your instructor rides alongside the whole way, so first-timers ride with confidence even on the long stretch to Promthep Cape." },
      { question: "Is hotel pickup included, or do I meet at Patong Beach?", answer: "This experience is based at **Patong Beach**, where you'll meet the operator's team, complete your briefing and collect your WaveRunner. Hotel pickup is not part of the standard booking, but Patong is central and easily reached by taxi, tuk-tuk or Grab from most west-coast hotels. If you're staying further afield, allow travel time so you arrive relaxed before your slot." },
      { question: "What is the minimum age, and can I bring a child or a passenger?", answer: "Adults and confident teens ride best, and the **Duo Jet Ski Rental — $105** is built for two riders sharing one WaveRunner, which is ideal for a parent riding with an older child or a nervous partner. Very young children can't drive, so families often prefer the duo set-up or the guided tour where the pace is managed. Message us with your group's ages before booking and we'll confirm the safest arrangement." },
      { question: "What should I wear and bring for the ride?", answer: "Wear **swimwear with a rash guard or T-shirt**, plus reef-safe sunscreen — the Andaman sun is strong and you'll be fully exposed on the water. Bring a towel and a change of clothes since you'll get soaked, especially on the 3-hour tour with its swimming stop at Promthep Cape. Leave phones and valuables in a dry bag or with the base; secure any glasses with a strap." },
      { question: "How physically demanding is the jet ski tour?", answer: "It's moderately active rather than strenuous — you'll grip the handlebars, brace against chop and use your core and arms to stay balanced, which most reasonably fit adults handle easily. The **3-hour guided ride to Promthep Cape** is longer, so expect tired arms and a bit of stiffness afterward. The short 30-minute rentals are gentle and great if you'd rather keep it brief." },
      { question: "What happens at the Promthep Cape swimming stop?", answer: "On the guided island hopping tour you'll pause near **Promthep Cape**, Phuket's dramatic southern headland, to cool off with a swim in the clear Andaman water and catch your breath after the long ride down the coast. **Drinking water** is provided at the stop. It's the scenic highlight of the route and a perfect photo moment before you turn back toward Patong." },
      { question: "When is the best time of day and year to go?", answer: "Morning and late-afternoon slots offer softer light and calmer seas, making the long run past Karon and Kata beaches smoother and cooler. The best conditions fall in Phuket's **dry season, roughly November to April**, when the Andaman is flat and clear. During the May–October monsoon the west coast can get choppy and rides may be paused for safety, so book flexible dates in those months." },
      { question: "Is jet skiing in Phuket safe, and what safety measures are in place?", answer: "Yes — every rider gets a **fitted life jacket and a full safety briefing** before setting off, and the Yamaha WaveRunners are well maintained. On the guided tour a professional guide leads the group and keeps everyone together across the open stretches to Promthep Cape. Follow your guide's speed and distance instructions, and inspect and photograph the ski at handover so any pre-existing marks are noted." },
      { question: "Can I take photos or video during the ride?", answer: "Absolutely — the coastline past Paradise and Freedom beaches and around Laem Krating headland is stunning. For safety you shouldn't hold a phone while driving, so a **strapped action camera (like a GoPro) mounted on the handlebars** or your chest is the way to go. The Promthep Cape swimming stop is the easiest moment to hand your phone to the guide for a proper photo." },
      { question: "How does the tour compare to Phuket's boat trips to the islands?", answer: "This is a fast, self-driven coastal ride hugging Phuket's own west coast, not a boat day-trip to distant islands. If you'd rather relax and reach further afield, consider the [Phi Phi Islands premium catamaran tour with Maya Bay and snorkeling](/thailand/phuket/phi-phi-islands-speedboat-tour-maya-bay-snorkeling) or a laid-back [private half-day yacht cruise to Phi Phi and Maya Bay](/thailand/phuket/phi-phi-islands-private-yacht-cruise-maya-bay). Many travelers pair a jet ski morning with a boat trip on another day." },
      { question: "What else can I do near Patong to round out my day?", answer: "Patong is packed with activities, so it's easy to build a full day around your ride. Adrenaline fans often add the [Hanuman World luge ride and zipline adventure](/thailand/phuket/hanuman-world-phuket-adventure-tour) or a beginner-friendly [Muay Thai training class](/thailand/phuket/muay-thai-training-class-phuket-beginners). If you'd rather slow down afterward, a [hands-on Thai cooking class and market tour](/thailand/phuket/thai-cooking-class-phuket-kata) is a great evening follow-up." },
      { question: "How do I book and confirm my jet ski slot?", answer: "Just select your option — the **$259 guided tour** or one of the rentals from **$69** — and your preferred date online, and you'll receive a confirmation. Because the operator runs limited WaveRunners per slot, weekends and dry-season peaks fill up, so booking a day or two ahead is wise. If your dates are flexible, tell us and we'll help slot you into the calmest conditions." },
      { question: "What is the cancellation policy if the weather turns bad?", answer: "Jet skiing depends on safe sea conditions, so if the operator cancels your slot because of rough monsoon swell or storms, you'll be offered a **reschedule or a full refund**. For personal cancellations we recommend booking with our flexible option and giving as much notice as possible. If you're unsure about the forecast, reach out and we'll advise on the best window before you commit." },
    ];
  }

  // --- REMAINING: agra-gatimaan-express-tour (auto-added 2026-07-02) ---
  if (slug === 'agra-gatimaan-express-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What exactly is included in the $65 Gatimaan Express option, and what isn't?", answer: "The headline **$65 Gatimaan Express option** covers confirmed Chair Car (Chair Car / CC) train tickets both ways (Delhi to Agra and back), an AC car to and from Agra Cantt station, and an **approved tour guide**. Importantly, **monument entry tickets and lunch are NOT included** in this particular option, so you'll pay the Taj Mahal and Agra Fort admission on site. If you'd rather have everything bundled, see the next FAQ about the all-inclusive choice." },
      { question: "Which option should I pick if I want entry tickets and lunch already paid for?", answer: "Choose the **All Inclusive CC 2nd Class Train Tickets with Car, Guide, Entry Ticket & 5 Star Lunch at $95**. This is the only option here that bundles your Taj Mahal and Agra Fort admission plus a **5-star lunch**, so there's nothing extra to sort out at the monuments. The $65 Gatimaan and the $65 CC 2nd Class options give you train, car and guide but leave tickets and food out." },
      { question: "What's the difference between the four options on this page?", answer: "The **$40 'Tour In Agra with Car, Driver and Guide'** is for travellers already in Agra (no train). The **$65 Gatimaan Express** and **$65 CC 2nd Class** options both add round-trip train tickets, car and guide but exclude entry tickets and lunch. The **$95 All Inclusive** adds the monument tickets and a 5-star lunch on top. Pick based on whether you need the train and whether you want tickets and food handled for you." },
      { question: "What time does the day begin and end?", answer: "It's an early start: the driver collects you from your Delhi/NCR hotel around **06:00 AM**, the Gatimaan Express departs Delhi at **08:10 AM** and reaches Agra Cantt at **09:50 AM**. You'll visit the Taj Mahal from about **10:15 AM**, Agra Fort from **12:30 PM**, and lunch around **02:00 PM** before the return train. It's a full same-day trip, so plan for a long but well-paced day back in Delhi by evening." },
      { question: "Is the Taj Mahal really skip-the-line on this tour?", answer: "Yes, the tour is built around **skip-the-line entry to both the Taj Mahal and Agra Fort**, so your guide walks you through the priority lane rather than the general queue. Note that on the $65 options you still purchase the entry ticket itself on site, while the $95 All Inclusive covers it. If you only need the fast-track ticket and no transport, the standalone [Taj Mahal Entry Ticket for foreigners](/india/agra/taj-mahal-entry-ticket) is a leaner option." },
      { question: "How fast is the Gatimaan Express and what's the ride like?", answer: "The **Gatimaan Express is India's fastest train**, covering Delhi to Agra in roughly **100 minutes** versus 3.5–4 hours by road. You travel in **Chair Car (CC) class**, an air-conditioned reserved coach, and a light breakfast is served on the morning run with a meal on the return. It's a comfortable, smooth way to reach Agra and skip the traffic-heavy highway drive." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or shared with strangers?", answer: "Sightseeing in Agra is by **private air-conditioned car** with your own driver and **approved guide**, so the on-ground portion is private to your party. The train itself is a scheduled public service, so your reserved Chair Car seats sit among other passengers. If you want a fully private overland alternative without the train, consider the [Delhi to Agra private day trip with transfers](/india/agra/taj-mahal-full-day-tour)." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and are there steps or climbs?", answer: "Expect a fair amount of walking on marble and stone at the **Taj Mahal** and across the ramps and courtyards of the **16th-century Agra Fort**, some of it on uneven ground. There are gentle inclines rather than steep staircases, but the complexes are large. Wear comfortable shoes and pace yourself, especially in summer heat; the guide keeps things steady and there are shaded rest spots along the way." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for kids and older travellers?", answer: "Yes, families and older travellers do this trip regularly. The **fast Gatimaan Express** avoids a tiring road journey, the sightseeing car is air-conditioned, and your guide sets the pace. The main considerations are the **06:00 AM pickup** and the walking distances at the monuments. For anyone with limited mobility, let us know in advance so the guide can plan shorter routes and more rest breaks." },
      { question: "What should I wear and when is the best time to visit?", answer: "Agra is hot from **April to June** (often 40°C+), pleasant and cool from **November to February**, and humid during the July–September monsoon. Light, breathable clothing, a hat, sunglasses and sunscreen are smart in the warmer months; carry a layer in winter mornings. Since the Taj Mahal is a monument, modest dress that covers shoulders and knees is respectful, and you'll remove shoes or wear provided covers on the marble platform." },
      { question: "Is lunch vegetarian-friendly, and what about the 5-star meal?", answer: "The lunch break is at a **5-star hotel** serving traditional Indian cuisine, and Indian menus are famously **vegetarian-friendly**, with plenty of vegan and Jain-suitable choices available on request. Remember lunch is only included in the **$95 All Inclusive option**; on the $65 options you cover your own meal. Mention any dietary needs or allergies when booking so the restaurant can prepare accordingly." },
      { question: "Do you get time to photograph the Taj Mahal?", answer: "Absolutely. Your guide knows the classic vantage points, from the front reflecting pool to the side angles, and can take your photos so everyone's in the shot. Golden morning light around your **10:15 AM** arrival is lovely for pictures. For a dedicated shoot with a specialist, the [Taj Mahal Photography Tour with a professional guide](/india/agra/taj-mahal-photography-tour) goes deeper into composition and timing." },
      { question: "What happens if the Gatimaan Express is delayed or I miss it?", answer: "Your seats are on **confirmed reserved (CNF) tickets**, and our team coordinates the timings closely, with the driver waiting at Agra Cantt to welcome you. In the rare event of a significant train delay or disruption on the day, the operator will assist with alternative arrangements to keep your sightseeing on track. We recommend arriving for the **06:00 AM pickup** promptly so there's a comfortable buffer before the 08:10 AM departure." },
      { question: "Is Agra safe, and will I be pestered by touts and vendors?", answer: "Agra is a well-visited tourist city and this tour is designed to keep things smooth. Around the Taj Mahal and Agra Fort you may encounter vendors and self-appointed 'guides', but having your own **approved guide** and private driver means you can politely decline and stay focused on the sights. A simple, firm 'no thank you' works well, and your guide will steer you past the busier touting spots." },
      { question: "How do I book and confirm, and what's the cancellation policy?", answer: "Book online by selecting your preferred option (Gatimaan $65, Agra-only $40, CC 2nd Class $65, or All Inclusive $95) and your travel date; because the train needs **confirmed reserved tickets**, we recommend booking a few days ahead so seats can be secured. You'll receive confirmation with pickup details for your Delhi/NCR hotel. For cancellation terms and any date-change flexibility, check the policy shown at checkout, as train-ticketing rules can differ from car-only tours." },
    ];
  }

  // --- REMAINING: india-gate-approved-guided-tour (auto-added 2026-07-02) ---
  if (slug === 'india-gate-approved-guided-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What exactly is included when I book this Delhi guide tour for $30?", answer: "The **$30 price covers a full 8-hour day with a Government-approved, English-speaking local guide** who walks you through both Old and New Delhi. If you add the car option, a private vehicle for the city tour is included too, so you're not hopping in and out of autos or the metro. The guide's expertise on Delhi's Seven Cities, from the Sultanate period to the Mughals and the British Raj, is really the heart of what you're paying for." },
      { question: "Does the price include monument entry tickets, like at the Red Fort or Qutub Minar?", answer: "No, **entry tickets to monuments are not included** in the $30 rate, and neither are meals. You'll pay entrance fees directly at each site you choose to enter (foreign-tourist rates apply at places like the Red Fort, Humayun's Tomb and Qutub Minar). Your guide will tell you the current fee at each stop and help you buy tickets quickly so you skip the confusion at the counter." },
      { question: "Is transport included, or do I need to arrange my own car?", answer: "Transport depends on the option you choose. The guide alone is included in the base rate, and a **car for the city tour is added only if you book that option**. If you'd rather have everything bundled with a premium vehicle, look at [Explore Old / New Delhi City, By Luxury Car & Official Tour Guide](/india/delhi/explore-old-new-delhi-city-luxury-car-tour) instead. Otherwise, your guide can happily navigate the metro and autos with you." },
      { question: "Do you offer hotel pickup, and where does the tour start?", answer: "With the car option, pickup and drop-off are typically arranged from your Delhi hotel so the 8 hours flow smoothly from door to door. If you take the guide-only option, you'll agree a convenient central meeting point, often near India Gate or Connaught Place, when you confirm your booking. Just share your hotel name and area after booking and the team will finalise the exact logistics with you." },
      { question: "Which sites will we actually visit in 8 hours?", answer: "There's no rigid checklist, which is the beauty of a private guide, but a full day usually blends **New Delhi's colonial landmarks (India Gate, Rashtrapati Bhavan, Humayun's Tomb, Qutub Minar) with Old Delhi's Mughal heart (Red Fort, Jama Masjid and the lanes of Chandni Chowk)**. Tell your guide what interests you most, whether that's Mughal architecture or Raj-era history, and they'll shape the day around it." },
      { question: "Can I customise the itinerary or focus on specific eras?", answer: "Absolutely, and that's why people choose a guide over a fixed coach tour. Since the day centres on Delhi's Seven Cities across the **Sultanate, Mughal and British Raj periods**, you can ask to lean into any one of them, spend longer at Old Delhi's bazaars, or slow down for photography. If you'd prefer a set structured route, the [Delhi Full Day Guided Tour](/india/delhi/delhi-full-day-guided-tour) is a good alternative." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or will I share it with strangers?", answer: "This is a **private experience with your own dedicated Government-approved guide**, not a shared group bus. The whole day is yours, so the pace, stops and conversation are tailored to you and your party. That makes it ideal for families, couples or solo travellers who want flexibility rather than being herded around on someone else's schedule." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and is it suitable for older travellers?", answer: "Expect a fair amount of walking, especially through Chandni Chowk's crowded lanes and around large complexes like the Red Fort and Qutub Minar, some with steps and uneven stone underfoot. With the **car option the walking is broken up by comfortable drives between sites**, which suits older travellers well. Tell your guide about any mobility concerns and they'll pace the day gently and skip anything too strenuous." },
      { question: "Is the tour good for kids?", answer: "Yes, a private guide is great with children because the pace bends to your family rather than the other way around. The **stories of emperors, forts and battles bring the monuments alive** in a way kids enjoy, and you can build in breaks for snacks or rest. With the car option, little ones can nap between stops and you avoid dragging them through the metro in the heat." },
      { question: "What's the best time of year and time of day to do this tour?", answer: "**October to March is by far the most comfortable window**, with pleasant, dry days ideal for a full 8 hours outdoors. Summers (April-June) are very hot, often above 40°C, and the monsoon (July-September) brings humidity and showers. Starting in the morning helps you cover Old Delhi before the midday heat and beat the worst of the Chandni Chowk crowds." },
      { question: "What should I wear and bring for the day?", answer: "Wear **comfortable closed walking shoes**, light breathable clothing, and carry a hat, sunglasses and plenty of water, especially in the warmer months. For Jama Masjid and other religious sites you'll need shoulders and knees covered, and you'll remove shoes before entering, so slip-ons are handy. A small amount of cash for entry tickets, snacks and any shopping is also worth having." },
      { question: "Can I take photographs at the monuments?", answer: "Yes, photography is welcome at most sites, and your guide knows the best angles for India Gate, Humayun's Tomb and the Qutub Minar. A few interiors or museums may charge a small camera fee or restrict shots, and your guide will flag those on the spot. The old lanes of Chandni Chowk are wonderfully photogenic, so keep your phone charged and ready." },
      { question: "Can I add shopping or street food to the day?", answer: "Definitely, your guide can steer you to Chandni Chowk's spice market and textile shops and point out trustworthy stalls, though meals and purchases are at your own cost. If shopping is your main interest, consider the dedicated [Delhi: Guided Shopping Tour Experience with Female Expert](/india/delhi/delhi-guided-shopping-tour-female-expert), or for Old Delhi's flavours the [Old Delhi Heritage Tour with Street Food](/india/delhi/jama-masjid-food-tour) is a delicious add-on." },
      { question: "Is it safe to explore Old Delhi with the guide?", answer: "Yes. Having a **Government-approved local guide is one of the safest ways to see Old Delhi**, as they know the lanes, keep you clear of touts and aggressive vendors, and help you navigate the crowds around Jama Masjid and Chandni Chowk with confidence. Keep valuables secure as you would in any busy city, and follow your guide's advice on where to walk and what to skip." },
      { question: "What's the cancellation policy and how do I confirm my booking?", answer: "Once you book, you'll receive a confirmation and the team will contact you to arrange your meeting point or hotel pickup and lock in whether you've taken the guide-only or car-included option. We recommend confirming your preferred start time and any special interests in advance so your guide can plan the route. For exact cancellation terms and any free-cancellation window, check the booking page or reach out to our team before you pay." },
      { question: "How does this compare to a Golden Triangle or Agra day trip from Delhi?", answer: "This tour is a **deep dive into Delhi itself over a single 8-hour day**, ideal if the capital is your focus. If you also want to see the Taj Mahal, a [Private Delhi to Agra Same Day Trip By Car](/india/delhi/private-taj-mahal-tour-from-delhi) works well as a separate day, while the [Golden Triangle 3 Days Tour](/india/delhi/golden-triangle-3-day-tour-from-delhi) adds Agra and Jaipur for a fuller India itinerary." },
    ];
  }

  // --- REMAINING: agra-professional-sunrise-tour (auto-added 2026-07-02) ---
  if (slug === 'agra-professional-sunrise-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "Is skip-the-line entry to the Taj Mahal included in this tour?", answer: "Yes. **Skip-the-line Taj Mahal entry is included**, so you won't queue with the general crowd at the gates. This is a real advantage at sunrise, when lines form early and every minute of soft golden light counts for your photos. Your guide handles the entry logistics so you can head straight in and start shooting." },
      { question: "What exactly do I take home from the photoshoot?", answer: "You receive **10 professionally edited photos with the Taj Mahal as your backdrop, delivered as both hard and soft copies**. A licensed professional photographer, booked in advance, shoots the session and provides pose guidance and creative angles. If you'd like more than the standard 10 frames, mention it to your photographer on the day so expectations are clear before you begin." },
      { question: "How long is the tour and what is the pace like?", answer: "The experience runs about **4 hours** and is priced at **$40 per person**. That window comfortably covers the optional cloth-shop stop for outfits, your photoshoot at the monument, and your guide walking you through the history and architecture afterward. It's an unhurried morning rather than a rushed tick-box visit, though sunrise means an early start." },
      { question: "Do you pick me up from my hotel?", answer: "Yes. Your tour guide **meets you at your Agra hotel** to begin the experience. From there you either stop at the cloth shop for traditional outfits or head directly to the Taj Mahal with your skip-the-line entry. Share your hotel name and room details when you book so the meeting time can be set around sunrise." },
      { question: "What is the traditional dress option and does it cost extra?", answer: "Before the shoot you can visit a cloth shop to rent a **sari with makeup for women and a Maharaja's robe for men**, which makes for striking, culturally rich photos in front of the white marble. This is offered on a **rental basis and is optional** — it's included only if you select that option. If you'd rather keep it simple, you can skip the shop and go straight to the monument." },
      { question: "Why book the sunrise slot instead of a daytime visit?", answer: "Sunrise gives you the **softest light and the smallest crowds** of the day, so the marble glows warm pink and gold and your background stays clear of other visitors. It's the photographer's favourite window for clean, luminous shots. If a guided daytime alternative suits your schedule better, the [Taj Mahal Photography Tour with a professional guide](/india/agra/taj-mahal-photography-tour) is worth a look." },
      { question: "Can I also visit Agra Fort as part of this tour?", answer: "Agra Fort is available as an **optional add-on** after your Taj Mahal photoshoot and history walk, rather than part of the core 4-hour itinerary. If seeing both is a priority, consider a dedicated combined itinerary such as the [Taj Mahal & Agra Fort Guided Tour](/india/agra/taj-mahal-agra-fort-guided-tour). Let your guide know in advance if you'd like to extend the morning." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for couples and honeymooners?", answer: "Absolutely — it's designed for **couples, honeymooners, and pre- and post-wedding shoots**, as well as families, solo travelers, and influencers. The private, personalized format means the photographer and guide focus entirely on you, guiding poses and framing for romantic, magazine-quality results. The traditional sari-and-robe option is especially popular with couples wanting a distinctive keepsake." },
      { question: "What should I wear and how hot does it get?", answer: "Agra summers are very hot, so if you're not renting traditional outfits, choose **light, breathable clothing and comfortable footwear** for walking on stone. Solid colours photograph beautifully against the white marble. **Water bottles and shoe covers are included**, and the shoe covers are required inside the mausoleum to protect the floors." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and is it okay for older travelers?", answer: "There's a fair bit of walking across the Taj Mahal complex on marble and stone surfaces, but a **golf cart is included** to help with the stretch to the monument, which eases the load. The pace is gentle and led by your guide, making it manageable for older travelers. Wear supportive shoes and take advantage of the included water on warm mornings." },
      { question: "Is the Taj Mahal open every day for this sunrise tour?", answer: "The Taj Mahal is open for sunrise every day **except Friday**, when the monument closes for prayers. If your only free day falls on a Friday, look at the [Agra Friday Special Tour covering the Fort, Baby Taj and Mehtab Bagh](/india/agra/agra-friday-tour-taj-closed-alternative) instead. Always confirm your date when booking so we can schedule around the closure." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or will I share it with strangers?", answer: "This is a **private, personalized experience** — the guide and professional photographer are dedicated to your group alone. That means the shoot moves at your rhythm, poses are tailored to you, and there are no strangers in your frames or slowing you down. It's one of the reasons the experience works so well for special occasions." },
      { question: "Can the photographer help me if I'm not used to being photographed?", answer: "Yes, that's a core part of the service. The photographer provides **pose guidance and creative photography angles**, so even if you feel awkward in front of a camera, you'll be gently directed into natural, flattering shots. Many guests arrive nervous and leave delighted with how relaxed the photos look." },
      { question: "Are children welcome on this tour?", answer: "Families are explicitly welcome, and children usually enjoy the golf-cart ride and the grandeur of the monument. The 4-hour, unhurried format leaves room for breaks, and included water bottles help on warm mornings. If you're traveling with little ones, let your guide know so the pace and any outfit choices can be adjusted." },
      { question: "How do I book and confirm my sunrise slot?", answer: "Book online and provide your **hotel name, travel date, and whether you want the traditional outfit option**, since the photographer is reserved in advance. Because the shoot is timed to sunrise, early confirmation helps us lock the exact meeting time. If you simply want entry without the photoshoot, the [Taj Mahal skip-the-line entry ticket for foreigners](/india/agra/taj-mahal-entry-ticket) is a leaner alternative." },
      { question: "What is the cancellation policy?", answer: "We recommend booking with flexibility in mind, as sunrise photoshoots depend on the photographer being reserved ahead of time and on the monument's Friday closure. Check the specific cancellation terms shown at checkout for your date, and reach out if your plans change so we can try to reschedule. Confirming early and communicating any changes promptly gives you the best outcome." },
    ];
  }

  // --- REMAINING: taj-mahal-approved-private-tour (auto-added 2026-07-02) ---
  if (slug === 'taj-mahal-approved-private-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "Where does this tour start, and can you pick me up from my Delhi hotel?", answer: "This is a **same-day trip from Delhi**, and your driver collects you directly from your preferred location in the morning. Pickup is available from **hotels, the railway station and the airport across Delhi, Gurgaon, Faridabad, Ghaziabad and Noida**. Just share your address when you book and the team will confirm a pickup time that leaves enough margin for the drive to Agra." },
      { question: "How long is the drive from Delhi to Agra, and what is the road like?", answer: "The journey to Agra takes **around 3 hours each way via the Yamuna Expressway** in a comfortable air-conditioned private car. The Expressway is a modern toll road, so it's a smooth ride. If you'd rather skip the road altogether, some travellers prefer the [Delhi–Agra round trip by Gatimaan Express train](/india/agra/delhi-agra-round-trip-gatimaan-train), which cuts the transfer time significantly." },
      { question: "Can we stop for breakfast or a toilet break on the way?", answer: "Absolutely. Just tell your driver if you need a **restroom stop or breakfast**, and he'll happily pull over at a suitable place along the Expressway. Because the car and driver are entirely private to your group, the pace is yours and there's no fixed roadside schedule to keep to." },
      { question: "Is the Taj Mahal entry ticket included in the price?", answer: "It depends on the option you choose. The **All Inclusive Tour with AC Car, Guide, Entry Fees & Lunch at 5 Star Hotel** covers your monument entrance fees, while the more basic transport-and-guide options do not. If you'd prefer to buy admission separately, you can arrange a standalone [Taj Mahal skip-the-line entry ticket for foreigners](/india/agra/taj-mahal-entry-ticket) instead." },
      { question: "What is the difference between the three booking options?", answer: "The **All Inclusive option** bundles the private AC car, government-approved guide, all monument entry fees and a **buffet lunch at a 5-star hotel** into one price. The **Tour with AC Car, Driver and Guide** option covers transport and guiding but leaves tickets and lunch to you. Choose the all-inclusive if you'd rather have everything sorted in advance with no queuing at ticket counters." },
      { question: "Is lunch provided, and can you cater for vegetarians?", answer: "A **buffet lunch at a 5-star restaurant is included when you select the All Inclusive option**. Indian buffets always feature a generous spread of vegetarian dishes, so vegetarians, vegans and those avoiding certain ingredients are very well looked after. Let the guide know of any dietary needs and he'll point you to suitable options at the buffet." },
      { question: "Do we get a real guide at the Taj Mahal, or just a driver?", answer: "You'll have a **private, government-approved guide who is a native of Agra** and joins you once you arrive in the city. Beyond skipping the ticket line, he shares the anecdotes and history behind Shah Jahan's monument to love that you'd otherwise miss. If you only need guiding and not transport, you can also [book an official Taj Mahal tour guide](/india/agra/taj-mahal-official-guided-tour) locally in Agra." },
      { question: "Besides the Taj Mahal, what else does the tour visit?", answer: "The itinerary also includes **Agra Fort, a UNESCO World Heritage Site**, the red-sandstone Mughal stronghold with sweeping views back toward the Taj. It makes a natural pairing with the mausoleum and rounds out the Mughal story of the city. Travellers wanting to add the abandoned imperial capital nearby might prefer the [Agra and Fatehpur Sikri day trip](/india/agra/taj-mahal-fatehpur-full-day-tour)." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and is the tour suitable for older travellers?", answer: "There's a fair amount of walking on marble and uneven stone, plus some steps at Agra Fort, but the pace is relaxed and private to your group. Helpfully, a **golf cart is included** to shuttle you between the outer gate and the Taj Mahal itself, which spares tired legs. Older travellers generally manage well, though comfortable shoes are essential." },
      { question: "Why do I need shoe covers, and are they provided?", answer: "Visitors must cover their footwear before stepping onto the white-marble plinth of the Taj Mahal to protect the surface. **Shoe covers are included** on this tour, so you don't need to remove your shoes or bring your own. You simply slip them on at the platform and carry on." },
      { question: "What should I wear and when is the best time to visit?", answer: "Agra is hot for much of the year, so **light, breathable clothing, a hat, sunglasses and sunscreen are wise**, especially from April to June when temperatures soar. The cooler, drier months of **October to March are the most comfortable** for sightseeing. Note the Taj Mahal is closed on Fridays, and on that day the [Agra Friday special tour of the Fort, Baby Taj and Mehtab Bagh](/india/agra/agra-friday-tour-taj-closed-alternative) is a great alternative." },
      { question: "Is this tour good for families with children?", answer: "Yes, the private format works well for families. Kids enjoy the golf-cart ride, the vast open courtyards of Agra Fort and the sheer scale of the Taj Mahal, and because it's your own car you can pause whenever little ones need a break. The included mineral water and flexible restroom stops make the long day much easier with children." },
      { question: "Can I take photos, and where are the best photo spots?", answer: "Photography is very welcome throughout the day. Classic shots include the Taj reflected in the long water channel and the framed view through the Great Gate, and your guide knows the best angles and quieter corners. Note that **tripods and photography inside the main mausoleum are restricted** by the monument authorities. Keen photographers may also like the dedicated [Taj Mahal photography tour with a professional guide](/india/agra/taj-mahal-photography-tour)." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or will I share the car with strangers?", answer: "This is a **fully private tour** for your group only, with a dedicated air-conditioned car, driver and government-approved guide. You won't share the vehicle with other travellers, and the schedule bends to your pace rather than a fixed group timetable." },
      { question: "What time will I get back to Delhi?", answer: "With around three hours of driving in each direction plus your time at the Taj Mahal, Agra Fort and lunch, this is a **full day out — expect to return to Delhi in the evening**. An early start makes the day far more comfortable, so plan a relaxed evening afterwards rather than another activity that same night." },
      { question: "How do I book and what is the cancellation policy?", answer: "Simply select your preferred option, choose your date and share your Delhi pickup location to confirm. Once your booking is processed you'll receive confirmation with your pickup details. For the exact cancellation and refund terms that apply to your chosen date, please check the policy shown at checkout before you pay, as timings can vary by season." },
    ];
  }

