  if (slug === 'city-palace-heritage-full-day-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What exactly does this full-day tour cover?", answer: "This is a **10-hour private guided tour** centred on the magnificent **City Palace Udaipur**, one of the largest palace complexes in Rajasthan, where you'll explore its grand courtyards, intricate balconies and royal museums. You'll also take in panoramic views over Lake Pichola and have time to shop for handicrafts, miniatures and local souvenirs. A government-approved local guide accompanies you throughout the day." },
      { question: "Is hotel pickup and drop-off included?", answer: "Yes. **Hotel and airport pickup and drop-off are included** in the price. Your day starts with a comfortable pickup from your Udaipur hotel, where you'll meet your guide for a short introduction to the city before heading to the City Palace. Please share your hotel name and room details when booking so the driver can find you." },
      { question: "How much does the tour cost and what does the price include?", answer: "The tour is priced at **$50 per person** for the full 10-hour experience. This covers your private air-conditioned car with driver, a government-approved local guide, all toll taxes and parking, a mineral water bottle, and lunch at a restaurant if you select that option. Note that **City Palace entry tickets are not listed as included**, so budget for the palace admission separately." },
      { question: "Are the City Palace entry tickets included in the $50 price?", answer: "The included list covers transport, your guide, tolls, parking, water and optional lunch, but **entrance fees for the City Palace and its museums are not explicitly included**. We recommend carrying some cash for the palace admission (and the optional Lake Pichola boat ride). Your guide will point you to the correct ticket counters and help you avoid queues." },
      { question: "Is the Lake Pichola boat ride part of the tour?", answer: "The **boat ride at Lake Pichola is optional** and not part of the core inclusions. If you choose it, you'll glide past iconic landmarks like Jag Mandir and the Lake Palace with beautiful views back toward the City Palace. It's one of the most memorable parts of an Udaipur visit, so it's well worth the extra ticket. If you'd like a version built around the lake, see the [Udaipur full-day sightseeing tour](/india/udaipur/lake-pichola-full-day-tour)." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or will I share it with strangers?", answer: "This is a **fully private tour** with your own air-conditioned car, driver and dedicated guide, so the pace is set entirely by your group. There are no strangers joining you. If you'd prefer a flexible private option with the choice of a half or full day, the [private sightseeing tour with an approved guide](/india/udaipur/city-palace-sightseeing-full-day-tour) is a good alternative." },
      { question: "How much walking is involved, and is the tour physically demanding?", answer: "The City Palace is a large complex with **several staircases, ramps and uneven stone floors**, so expect a fair amount of walking and some climbing to reach the upper terraces and viewpoints. It's manageable for most reasonably mobile visitors, but there are narrow passages and steps that aren't wheelchair-friendly. Comfortable, closed walking shoes make a big difference." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for children and older travellers?", answer: "Yes, the private format works well for **families and older travellers** because you control the pace and the car is on hand between stops. Kids usually enjoy the courtyards, the palace museums and the optional boat ride. For seniors, take the stairs slowly and rest on the terraces; your guide can adjust the route to avoid the steepest sections if needed." },
      { question: "What time does the tour start and how is the day paced?", answer: "The **full day runs about 10 hours** starting with a morning hotel pickup, which lets you reach the City Palace before the midday heat and crowds build. The private pace means you can linger in the museums, break for lunch, and add the optional boat ride at golden hour. Let us know if you'd prefer a specific start time and we'll try to accommodate it." },
      { question: "When is the best time of year to visit Udaipur for this tour?", answer: "The most comfortable months are **October to March**, when Udaipur's days are pleasantly warm and evenings cool. April to June brings intense heat that can make the palace walking tiring, while the July-September monsoon brings lush scenery and occasional showers. Whatever the season, an early start helps you enjoy the City Palace before it gets busy." },
      { question: "What should I wear and bring for the day?", answer: "Wear **light, breathable clothing and comfortable closed walking shoes** for the stone staircases, plus a hat and sunglasses for the open terraces. As the City Palace is a heritage and partly religious site, modest dress covering shoulders and knees is respectful. A mineral water bottle is provided, but bring sunscreen, some cash for entry tickets and the optional boat ride, and your camera." },
      { question: "Can I take photographs inside the City Palace?", answer: "Yes, **photography is very much part of the experience** here, from the mirrored and mosaic chambers to the sweeping views over Lake Pichola and the old city rooftops. Some museum galleries may charge a small camera fee or restrict photography, and your guide will let you know where. Mornings and late afternoon give the softest light for palace and lake shots." },
      { question: "Will there be time for shopping, and should I bargain?", answer: "Yes, the itinerary includes time to **shop for handicrafts, miniature paintings and local souvenirs**, which Udaipur is famous for. In the markets and independent shops, **friendly bargaining is expected and normal** — starting around half the asking price is common. Your guide can point you toward reputable sellers so you get authentic pieces at fair prices." },
      { question: "Is lunch included and are vegetarian options available?", answer: "**Lunch at a restaurant is included only if you select that option** when booking; otherwise you're free to eat wherever you like during the break. Udaipur has excellent Rajasthani cuisine, and **vegetarian food is abundant and often the default**, with plenty of Jain and mild options too. Tell your guide about any dietary needs and they'll recommend a suitable spot." },
      { question: "How do I book, and can I combine this with day trips near Udaipur?", answer: "Simply book online and you'll receive confirmation with pickup details; share your hotel name so the driver can collect you. If you have more time, Udaipur is a great base for excursions — consider the [Kumbhalgarh and Ranakpur temple round trip](/india/udaipur/ranakpur-jain-temple-spiritual-tour) or the [Chittorgarh Fort day trip by car](/india/udaipur/chittorgarh-fort-full-day-tour) to pair majestic forts and temples with your city day." },
    ];
  }

