  if (slug === 'sarangkot-sunrise-tour') {
    return [
      { question: "What time does the Sarangkot Sunrise Tour start, and why so early?", answer: "Pickup is very early, typically around **4:30 to 5:00 AM** from your hotel in Lakeside, so you reach the Sarangkot viewpoint before first light. The whole point is to be in position as the sun rises and paints the Annapurna Range gold, which happens shortly after dawn. Exact pickup time shifts slightly by season, and your guide will confirm it the evening before." },
      { question: "How long is the tour and what is the pace like?", answer: "The experience runs about **3 hours** in total, door to door. That includes the short drive up to Sarangkot, time at the viewpoint to enjoy sunrise and photos, and the return to your hotel. It is a relaxed, easy-going morning rather than a rushed schedule, so you have room to soak in the panorama and take your pictures." },
      { question: "Does the tour involve any hiking or a difficult climb?", answer: "No strenuous trekking is required, which is exactly what makes this tour so popular. A **private A/C tourist vehicle** drives you almost all the way up to the viewpoint at 1,600 meters. There is only a short, gentle walk of a few minutes from the parking area to the main viewing platform, over some steps and paved paths." },
      { question: "Is this a private tour or shared with other travelers?", answer: "This is a **private tour** with your own dedicated air-conditioned tourist vehicle. You will not be sharing the ride with strangers, so pickup, pace and photo stops revolve around your group. It is a comfortable, personal way to experience the Sarangkot sunrise, especially with an early start." },
      { question: "What exactly is included in the $30 price?", answer: "The **Sarangkot Sunrise** option is priced at **$30** and includes your private A/C tourist vehicle with hotel pickup in Lakeside and return. It covers the round-trip transport and your time at the viewpoint. Any personal expenses, tips, or optional hot tea at the summit stalls are not included." },
      { question: "Is there an entry ticket to Sarangkot, and is it covered?", answer: "Sarangkot has a small local viewpoint entry fee that visitors pay on site. The listed **$30** option covers your private transport and pickup rather than the modest ticket, so bring a little Nepali cash for the entrance. It is only a few hundred rupees and is paid directly at the top." },
      { question: "Which mountains will I actually be able to see from Sarangkot?", answer: "On a clear morning you get sweeping views of the **Annapurna Range**, with peaks like Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Annapurna South and Dhaulagiri catching the first light. You will also look down over the **Pokhara Valley** and the calm waters of **Phewa Lake**. Visibility depends on the weather, but early mornings offer the clearest skies." },
      { question: "What is the best season for clear sunrise views?", answer: "The clearest mountain views usually come between **October and April**, with autumn and winter offering crisp, cloud-free mornings. The monsoon months of June to September can bring haze and cloud that occasionally hide the peaks. That said, sunrise over the valley is atmospheric year-round, and mist can add its own drama." },
      { question: "What should I wear and bring for the early morning?", answer: "Mornings at 1,600 meters are chilly even in warmer seasons, so dress in **warm layers**, including a jacket, and add a hat and gloves in winter. Comfortable shoes help for the short walk to the viewpoint. Bring your camera, a little cash for the entry fee and tea, and perhaps a small flashlight for the pre-dawn arrival." },
      { question: "Is the tour suitable for children and older travelers?", answer: "Yes. Because there is **no demanding trek** and the vehicle drives most of the way up, this tour works well for families with children and for older travelers. The only effort is a short walk to the platform. The main consideration is the very early wake-up, so plan an early night beforehand." },
      { question: "Is Sarangkot good for photography?", answer: "It is one of the best sunrise photography spots in Pokhara. The light on the **Annapurna peaks**, the layered valley below and Phewa Lake in the distance make for stunning shots. Arriving before dawn lets you set up for the changing colors as the sun climbs, so bring a fully charged camera or phone and a spare battery for the cold." },
      { question: "How long is the drive up to the viewpoint?", answer: "The drive from Lakeside up to Sarangkot is short, roughly **30 to 45 minutes** depending on road conditions and your hotel location. The final stretch is winding and uphill, but your private A/C vehicle keeps it comfortable. This easy access is a big part of why the tour is so appealing compared to a full trek." },
      { question: "Can I combine this with other adventures in Pokhara?", answer: "Absolutely. Many travelers pair the sunrise with an adrenaline activity later in the day, since Sarangkot is also a launch point for adventure sports. A popular choice is [Pokhara: Tandem Paragliding with Annapurna Views](/nepal/pokhara/sarangkot-guided-tour), which lets you soar over Phewa Lake with the same mountain backdrop. Just leave a gap after your early morning to rest." },
      { question: "What happens if the weather is cloudy or it rains?", answer: "Sarangkot is beautiful even under cloud, with mist drifting through the valley, so the tour typically runs as planned. Mountain visibility can never be guaranteed on any given morning. If you are chasing peak clarity, book across a season like autumn or winter and, where possible, choose a morning with a promising forecast." },
      { question: "How do I book and confirm this tour?", answer: "You can reserve directly through AsiaByLocals by selecting the **Sarangkot Sunrise** option at **$30** and providing your Lakeside hotel details for pickup. Once confirmed, we will share your exact early-morning pickup time. If your plans change, contact us in advance about the cancellation terms so we can help adjust your booking." },
    ];
  }

