  if (slug === "doi-inthanon-national-park-guided-tour") {
    return [
      { question: "When is the best time to see the Pa Bong Piang rice terraces?", answer: "The terraces look completely different depending on the month, so timing matters. From **June to October** they're lush and **emerald green**, while **November to early December** brings the short-lived **golden harvest season** many photographers chase. By **January onward** the fields are dry and harvested, so if the terraces themselves are your main goal, aim for the green or golden window rather than the dry months." },
      { question: "How cold does it get at the summit of Doi Inthanon?", answer: "As Thailand's highest point, the summit area around the twin pagodas and Ang Ka nature trail sits at roughly **2,565 meters**, so temperatures can drop to **10-15\u00b0C (50-59\u00b0F)** even in the hot season, and colder in December-January mornings. It's a sharp contrast to Chiang Mai city, so **bring a light jacket or fleece** \u2014 layers are the easiest fix since it warms up again lower down." },
      { question: "Is this tour suitable for older travelers or families with kids?", answer: "Yes, it's generally family- and senior-friendly since most highlights (the pagodas, viewpoints, and village visit) involve **short walks on paved or well-maintained paths** rather than technical hiking. The **9.5-hour duration** with a lot of driving is the main consideration, so travelers who tire on long days should pace themselves and bring snacks and water for the ride between stops." },
      { question: "What exactly is included in the $85 price?", answer: "The rate covers **round-trip transport from Chiang Mai**, an **English-speaking guide**, **lunch**, and **all entrance fees** for Doi Inthanon National Park and its attractions, so there are no separate ticket lines to manage on the day. It's a **single all-inclusive option** at $85 per person, with **free cancellation up to 24 hours before** the tour." },
      { question: "How difficult is the hiking on this tour?", answer: "Overall it's an **easy-to-moderate** day out. The **Ang Ka cloud forest nature trail** is a short boardwalk loop through moss-covered forest, and the Mae Klang Luang village walk is gentle and flat, while the main physical challenge is simply the altitude and cool air rather than steep terrain. **No prior hiking experience or special fitness is needed.**" },
      { question: "Does the tour visit the rice terraces themselves or just a viewpoint?", answer: "The tour includes a stop at the **Pa Bong Piang viewpoint**, which offers sweeping views over the stepped terraces built into the hillside, plus time in the nearby **Karen village of Mae Klang Luang**, which itself sits amid smaller terraced plots. It's a scenic overlook and village experience rather than a working-farm walking tour, so expect **photo stops** more than trekking through the paddies." },
      { question: "Is Doi Inthanon crowded, and does the tour avoid the crowds?", answer: "The summit and twin pagodas are popular with both tourists and local visitors, especially on **weekends and Thai holidays**, so those two spots can feel busy. Guides typically plan the **route order to beat tour-bus peaks**, and quieter stops like Mae Klang Luang village and the Ang Ka trail tend to stay noticeably calmer than the summit area." },
    ];
  }
